+# Windows Setup Guide
+
+Setup and run instructions for the **NW Agentic Tools Monorepo** on Windows.
+For the cross-platform overview and architecture, see [`README.md`](README.md).
+
+> **The repo's shell scripts (`scripts/*.sh`) are bash-only.** On Windows you have
+> two options:
+>
+> 1. **WSL2 / Git Bash (recommended)** — run everything exactly as the README shows,
+>    including `./scripts/bootstrap.sh` and `bash scripts/generate_grpc.sh`.
+> 2. **Native PowerShell** — follow this guide. A PowerShell port of the gRPC
+>    codegen is provided at [`scripts/generate_grpc.ps1`](scripts/generate_grpc.ps1);
+>    the other `.sh` scripts (scaffolders, coverage) still require Git Bash/WSL.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Prerequisites
+
+| Tool | Version | Install |
+|------|---------|---------|
+| **Python** | **3.12.0** on Windows (`.python-version` pins 3.12) | [python.org 3.12.0](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3120/) or `winget install Python.Python.3.12` |
+| **uv** | latest | `winget install astral-sh.uv` or `pip install uv` |
+| **Node.js** | 20+ | `winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS` |
+| **pnpm** | 9+ | `npm install -g pnpm` |
+| **PowerShell** | 7+ (`pwsh`) | `winget install Microsoft.PowerShell` |
+
+Verify:
+
+```powershell
+python --version   # Python 3.12.x
+uv --version
+node --version
+pnpm --version
+```
+
+> The document-data-extractor pulls heavy native ML/vision wheels
+> (PyMuPDF, OpenCV-contrib, python-doctr[torch], img2table). These install fine
+> on Windows but are large; skip that package if you only need the transaction agents.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Bootstrap (preferred: uv workspace)
+
+From the repo root in **PowerShell**:
+
+```powershell
+# 1. Sync the whole uv workspace (all Python packages, editable)
+uv sync --all-packages
+
+# 2. Install JS/TS workspace deps (UI libs + web apps)
+pnpm install
+
+# 3. Generate gRPC stubs — REQUIRED before starting any business agent.
+#    (Agents fail with "No module named ...channels.grpc.generated" without this.)
+pwsh -File scripts/generate_grpc.ps1
+```
+
+> ⚠️ Do **not** run `uv run pip install -e .` at the root — the root is a uv
+> workspace hub, not an installable package (see `pyproject.toml`).
+
+### Alternative: pip + requirements.txt (no uv)
+
+A pip fallback is provided in [`requirements.txt`](requirements.txt) (third-party deps only).
+You must still install the local workspace packages editable afterwards:
+
+```powershell
+python -m venv .venv
+.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+
+# Install the local (non-PyPI) workspace packages editable, dependency order first:
+pip install -e libs/common/core `
+            -e libs/agents/toolkit `
+            -e agents/core/bank-transactions `
+            -e agents/core/document-data-extractor `
+            -e agents/business/salary-extractor `
+            -e agents/business/rent-extractor `
+            -e agents/business/gift-extractor `
+            -e agents/business/property-sale-extractor `
+            -e tests
+
+pwsh -File scripts/generate_grpc.ps1
+```
+
+> If PowerShell blocks `Activate.ps1`, run once:
+> `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned`.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Environment
+
+Set `NW_ENV` to select which `config/env.{NW_ENV}` each component loads
+(default `dev`). All `pnpm dev:*` scripts already pass `--env dev`.
+
+```powershell
+$env:NW_ENV = "dev"   # dev | qa | uat | prod
+```
+
+---
+
+## 4. Run the REST APIs (via package.json)
+
+The `pnpm dev:*` scripts work identically on Windows (they shell out to `uv run`).
+Run each from the repo root; it stays in the foreground (Ctrl+C to stop).
+
+| Agent | Command | REST port | gRPC port |
+|-------|---------|-----------|-----------|
+| Echo (sample) | `pnpm dev:echo:rest` | 8001 | — |
+| Bank-transactions (core, 12-phase) | `pnpm dev:bank-transactions:rest` | 8010 | — |
+| Document-data-extractor (core, OCR) | `pnpm dev:document-data-extractor:rest` | 8080 | — |
+| **Salary extractor** | `pnpm dev:salary-extractor:rest` | 8020 | 5020 |
+| **Rent extractor** | `pnpm dev:rent-extractor:rest` | 8021 | 5021 |
+| **Gift extractor** | `pnpm dev:gift-extractor:rest` | 8022 | 5022 |
+| **Property-sale extractor** | `pnpm dev:property-sale-extractor:rest` | 8023 | 5023 |
+| Template API (FastAPI) | `pnpm dev:app:api` | 8080 |
+| Template web (Next.js) | `pnpm dev:app:web` | 3000 |
+
+### Smoke-test an endpoint
+
+Every business agent exposes `POST /api/v1/<profile>/detect`. Example against the
+salary agent (PowerShell `Invoke-RestMethod`):
+
+```powershell
+$body = @{
+  analysis_id    = "realworld_01_missing_transaction_list"
+  validation_mode= "lenient"
+  transactions   = @()
+  country_region = "EnglandAndWales"
+  jurisdiction   = "GB"
+} | ConvertTo-Json
+
+Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8020/api/v1/salary/detect" `
+  -ContentType "application/json" -Body $body | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10
+```
+
+Or with `curl.exe` (note the `.exe` — bare `curl` is a PowerShell alias for `Invoke-WebRequest`):
+
+```powershell
+curl.exe -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8022/api/v1/gift/detect `
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" `
+  -d '{ \"analysis_id\": \"smoke_gift\", \"validation_mode\": \"lenient\", \"transactions\": [], \"country_region\": \"EnglandAndWales\", \"jurisdiction\": \"GB\" }'
+```
+
+> **Detector inputs differ:** `salary` and `rent` run on transaction signals alone;
+> `gift` and `property-sale` **require** a hint block (`gift_hints` / `sale_hints`)
+> and will return a `MISSING_*_AMOUNT` warning otherwise. See each agent's README
+> for the full request shape. Endpoint paths: `/api/v1/{salary,rent,gift,property-sale}/detect`.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Testing
+
+All test commands run via `uv run` under the hood and work in PowerShell.
+
+### Unit / marker suites (package.json wrappers)
+
