+# gRPC channel — gift extractor
+
+Naming and codegen conventions for this agent's gRPC surface.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+channels/grpc/
+├── proto/nw/gift/v1/gift_extractor.proto   # hand-written contract (snake_case paths)
+├── generated/nw/gift/v1/                     # protoc output — do not edit
+│   ├── gift_extractor_pb2.py
+│   └── gift_extractor_pb2_grpc.py
+├── Converters.py                             # proto ↔ domain (PascalCase)
+├── Servicer.py                               # GiftExtractorServicer (PascalCase)
+└── GrpcRegistry.py                           # server registration
+```
+
+## Naming policy
+
+| Layer | Convention | Examples |
+|-------|------------|----------|
+| **Hand-written Python** | PascalCase module filenames | `Converters.py`, `Servicer.py`, `GrpcRegistry.py` |
+| **Proto files** | snake_case path + message names | `gift_extractor.proto`, `DetectGiftCandidatesRequest` |
+| **Generated Python** | protoc defaults (snake_case modules) | `gift_extractor_pb2.py`, `gift_extractor_pb2_grpc.py` |
+| **RPC methods** | PascalCase in `.proto` (gRPC style) | `DetectGiftCandidates` |
+
+Do **not** rename generated `*_pb2*.py` files or proto package paths — tooling and import fixups in `scripts/generate_grpc.sh` depend on the current layout.
+
+## Codegen
+
+From the repo root:
+
+```bash
+./scripts/generate_grpc.sh
+```
+
+This regenerates:
+
+- shared `nw_core` stubs (`common.proto`, `hints.proto`, `results.proto`)
+- this agent's stubs under `channels/grpc/generated/`
+
+Edit only `proto/` and hand-written modules; commit regenerated output when the contract changes.
+
+## Shared helpers
+
+Detect RPC handlers use `nw_aglib_toolkit.channels.grpc.DetectRpc` for request parsing, config/calendar context, and error/success response shaping — keep servicer methods thin.
+
+## Testing
+
+```bash
+uv run --package nw-agbus-gift-extractor pytest agents/business/gift-extractor/tests/unit -m unit -k grpc
+uv run --package nw-agbus-gift-extractor pytest agents/business/gift-extractor/tests/feature/GrpcDetectTest.py -m feature
+```
