+# Rent Transaction Extractor Service
+
+**Module:** `nw_agbus_rent_extractor.services`  
+**Orchestrator:** `RentTransactionExtractorService.detect`  
+**Role:** End-to-end UK rental-income detection — recurrence-based candidate generation (skeleton + graph) with rent-specific hints, stream recovery, and `run_score_recurrence_pool(profile="rent")`.
+
+Package overview: [`../README.md`](../README.md).
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Purpose and system position](#purpose-and-system-position)
+- [Entry points](#entry-points)
+- [Inputs and outputs](#inputs-and-outputs)
+- [Orchestration flow](#orchestration-flow)
+- [Business logic algorithm](#business-logic-algorithm)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Request parsing](#request-parsing)
+- [REST sequence diagram](#rest-sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+
+---
+
+## Purpose and system position
+
+The rent extractor detects **recurring rental-income credit streams** on UK bank statements. It is a sibling to the salary extractor but follows the **recurrence scoring path** rather than the full salary pipeline (no bonus/expense split, no employment transition).
+
+| Layer | Responsibility |
+|-------|----------------|
+| **Core pipeline** | Validation, normalisation, features, skeleton/graph clustering, dedup, fallback |
+| **This service** | Rent hint applicator, `_recover_distinct_rent_streams`, rent YAML weights, recurrence scoring profile |
+| **Channels** | REST `/rent/detect`, `@tool detect_rent_candidates`, optional gRPC |
+
+Rent reuses skeleton and graph phases from core bank-transactions but applies rent-specific description signals, hint matching, and scoring weights from `rent_detector.yaml`.
+
+---
+
+## Entry points
+
+### Tool (`@tool`)
+
+```python
+from nw_agbus_rent_extractor.channels.tools.RentTransactionExtractorTools import (
+    detect_rent_candidates,
+)
+from nw_agbus_rent_extractor.services import BankTransactionRequest
+
+result = detect_rent_candidates(payload, include_audit=False)
+```
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Tool name | `detect_rent_candidates` |
+| Category | `banking.rent` |
+| Wrapper class | `RentTransactionExtractorTools` |
+
+### REST
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/rent/detect` |
+| Route class | `RentDetectRoute` |
+| Request model | `DetectRentRequest` |
+| Response model | `DetectRentSuccessResponse` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/openapi/detect_rent_candidates.openapi.yaml` |
+
+### gRPC
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Service | `nw.rent.v1.RentExtractor` |
+| RPC | `DetectRentCandidates` |
+| Servicer | `RentExtractorServicer` |
+| Proto | `channels/grpc/proto/nw/rent/v1/rent_extractor.proto` |
+
+---
+
+## Inputs and outputs
+
+### Request — `BankTransactionRequest`
+
+Same shared DTO as salary. Rent-specific data lives in `hint_inputs.rent_hints`.
+
+### Hint block — `rent_hints`
+
+| Field | Required | Default | Purpose |
+|-------|----------|---------|---------|
+| `amount` | No | — | Expected rent amount (integer-part match by default) |
+| `tolerance_pct` | No | **0%** | Symmetric ±% band around `amount` |
+| `rentee_name` | No | — | Token overlap (exact/partial, same as employer hints) |
+| `property_ref` | No | — | Property reference token match |
+| `location` | No | — | Location substring hint |
+| `postcode` | No | — | Postcode token match |
+| `target_day_of_month` | No | **1** | Expected payment day |
+| `tolerance_days` | No | **±7** | Calendar-day window around target day |
+| `properties[]` | No | — | Multi-property landlord array (amount + metadata per property) |
+
+### Response — `BankTransactionResult`
+
+| Field | Rent-specific notes |
+|-------|---------------------|
+| `candidate_sets` | Ranked rent streams (`probable_rent`, `possible_rent` types from scoring) |
+| `rejected_or_near_miss_sets` | Below threshold, negative rent keywords, cap overflow |
+| `applied_hints` | `AppliedHints.rent` — amount matched, rentee match level, property hints |
+| `warnings` | Validation + `no_signal_detected` when fallback-only path |
+
