+
+## High-level design (HLD)
+
+### Purpose
+
+Accept bank transactions with optional salary, employer, and payslip hints; return ranked salary candidate sets with confidence, candidate types, reasoning, and optional audit snapshots. Runs **one end-to-end detect** per request (unlike the core agent, which exposes each phase independently).
+
+### System context
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TB
+    subgraph consumers [Consumers]
+        REST[REST clients]
+        TOOLS[LLM tool callers]
+        FEAT[tests/feature employment module]
+    end
+
+    subgraph salary [nw-agbus-salary-extractor]
+        CH[channels rest tools grpc]
+        ORCH[core Orchestrator]
+        SVC[SalaryTransactionExtractorService]
+        CH --> ORCH --> SVC
+    end
+
+    subgraph core [nw-agcore-bank-transactions]
+        PIPE[pipeline phases 1-12]
+    end
+
+    REST -->|POST /api/v1/salary/detect| CH
+    TOOLS -->|detect_salary_candidates| CH
+    FEAT --> SVC
+    SVC -->|run_* chain| PIPE
+```
+
+### Design principles
+
+| Principle | Implementation |
+|-----------|----------------|
+| Thin channels | REST/tools → `detect_salary_candidates` tool |
+| Core composition | Service imports `run_*` from core — no forked phase logic |
+| Composite deployment | `mode: composite`; suppresses duplicate core REST/tools |
+| Stateless REST | Per-request `RouteContext` via `BaseToolRoute` |
+
+### Channels (configured)
+
+From [`config/deployment.yaml`](config/deployment.yaml):
+
+| Channel | Enabled | Entry point |
+|---------|---------|-------------|
+| REST | ✅ | `POST /api/v1/salary/detect` |
+| Tools | ✅ | `detect_salary_candidates` |
+| gRPC | ❌ | `DetectSalaryCandidates` (wired when enabled) |
+| MQ | ❌ | Not registered |
+
