+# Salary Transaction Extractor Service
+
+**Module:** `nw_agbus_salary_extractor.services`  
+**Orchestrator:** `SalaryTransactionExtractorService.detect`  
+**Role:** End-to-end UK salary detection — composes the full 12-phase bank-transaction pipeline from [`nw-agcore-bank-transactions`](../../../../core/bank-transactions/) plus employment-transition linking and negative-keyword partitioning.
+
+Package overview: [`../README.md`](../README.md).
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Purpose and system position](#purpose-and-system-position)
+- [Entry points](#entry-points)
+- [Inputs and outputs](#inputs-and-outputs)
+- [Orchestration flow](#orchestration-flow)
+- [Business logic algorithm](#business-logic-algorithm)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Request parsing](#request-parsing)
+- [REST sequence diagram](#rest-sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+
+---
+
+## Purpose and system position
+
+The salary extractor is a **business agent orchestrator**. It does not reimplement pipeline phases; it chains `run_*` functions from the core bank-transactions package into a single deterministic `detect()` call suitable for REST, gRPC, LLM tools, and in-process use via `core.Orchestrator`.
+
+| Layer | Responsibility |
+|-------|----------------|
+| **Core pipeline** (`nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.*`) | Validation, normalisation, feature extraction, candidate generation, scoring, ranking |
+| **This service** | Salary-specific config overrides, description signals, 14-step orchestration, employment-transition merge, negative-keyword near-miss partition |
+| **Channels** (`channels/rest`, `channels/tools`, `channels/grpc`) | Transport adapters — parse request, build `RouteContext`, invoke `detect_salary_candidates` |
+
+Salary is the **reference full-pipeline path**. Rent reuses skeleton/graph phases with rent scoring; gift and property-sale use hint-grouping instead.
+
+---
+
+## Entry points
+
+### Tool (`@tool`)
+
+```python
+from nw_agbus_salary_extractor.channels.tools.SalaryTransactionExtractorTools import (
+    detect_salary_candidates,
+)
+from nw_agbus_salary_extractor.services import BankTransactionRequest
+
+result = detect_salary_candidates(payload, include_audit=False)
+```
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Tool name | `detect_salary_candidates` |
+| Category | `banking.salary` |
+| Wrapper class | `SalaryTransactionExtractorTools` |
+| TRACE logging | Linearised request JSON logged as `tool.request {...}` at TRACE level |
+
+### REST
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/salary/detect` |
+| Route class | `SalaryDetectRoute` |
+| Request model | `DetectSalaryRequest` (`channels/rest/ApiModels.py`) |
+| Response model | `DetectSalarySuccessResponse` (`channels/rest/ApiResponseModels.py`) |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/openapi/detect_salary_candidates.openapi.yaml` |
+
+### gRPC
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Service | `nw.salary.v1.SalaryExtractor` |
+| RPC | `DetectSalaryCandidates` |
+| Servicer | `SalaryExtractorServicer` |
+| Proto | `channels/grpc/proto/nw/salary/v1/salary_extractor.proto` |
+
+gRPC is optional — enabled via `config/deployment.yaml` channel toggles.
+
+### OpenAPI
+
+The OpenAPI spec is served from the agent REST router and documents the full request body including `salary_hints`, `employer_hints`, `transactions`, and ranking overrides (`max_candidates`, `return_threshold`, `include_audit`).
+
+---
+
+## Inputs and outputs
+
+### Request — `BankTransactionRequest`
+
+Shared DTO from `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline._models.requests`:
+
+| Field | Type | Purpose |
+|-------|------|---------|
+| `analysis_id` | `str` | Correlation id for logs and audit |
+| `transactions` | `tuple[RawBankTransaction, ...]` | Raw bank statement rows |
+| `jurisdiction` | `str` | Default `"GB"` |
+| `country_region` | `str \| None` | Calendar region override (`EnglandAndWales`, `Scotland`, …) |
+| `validation_mode` | `str` | `"lenient"` (default) or `"strict"` |
+| `hint_inputs` | `HintInputs` | Parsed hint blocks (see below) |
+| `transactions_range` | `TransactionsRange \| None` | Optional analysis window for coverage scoring |
+| `source_bank` | `str \| None` | Metadata only |
+
+### Hint blocks
+
+| Block | Key fields | Purpose |
+|-------|------------|---------|
+| `salary_hints` | `amount`, `tolerance_pct`, `payslip_date`, `tolerance_days` | Approx-salary band and payslip anchor |
+| `employer_hints` | `current_employer`, `previous_employer` | Token overlap bonus and match floors |
+
+Hints are applied in phase 4 via `run_apply_bank_transaction_hints`. See core [`pipeline/hints/`](../../../../core/bank-transactions/src/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/hints/) for matcher details.
+
+### Response — `BankTransactionResult`
+
+| Field | Purpose |
+|-------|---------|
+| `candidate_sets` | Ranked salary candidate sets above `return_threshold` |
+| `rejected_or_near_miss_sets` | Below-threshold, cap-overflow, and negative-keyword rejections |
+| `warnings` | Validation and pipeline warnings |
+| `applied_hints` | Payslip anchor and salary-band application summary |
+| `inferred_country_regions` | Regions inferred when `country_region` omitted |
+| `input_summary` | Transaction/credit counts and date range |
+| `metadata` | Effective thresholds, config versions, validation mode |
+| `audit` | Optional per-phase audit snapshot when `include_audit=True` |
+
+### Sample REST request
+
+```json
+{
+  "analysis_id": "demo",
+  "validation_mode": "lenient",
+  "transactions": [
+    {
+      "id": "t1",
+      "date": "2024-01-25",
+      "description": "ACME PAYROLL SALARY",
+      "credit_amount": "2500.00",
+      "debit_amount": 0
+    }
+  ],
+  "salary_hints": {
+    "amount": 2500,
+    "tolerance_pct": 0.05
+  },
+  "employer_hints": {
+    "current_employer": "ACME LTD"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## Orchestration flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[BankTransactionRequest] --> V[1 validation]
+    V -->|early_exit| OUT0[Empty BankTransactionResult]
+    V --> N[2 normalization]
+    N --> F[3 feature_extraction]
+    F --> H[4 salary hints]
+    H --> SK[5 skeleton_grouping]
+    H --> GR[6 graph_clustering]
+    SK --> DD[7 dedup_candidate_pool]
+    GR --> DD
+    DD --> BE[8 bonus_expense_split]
+    BE --> FB[9 amount_date_fallback]
+    FB --> SC[10 scoring]
+    SC --> ET[11 employment_transition]
+    ET --> NK[12 negative_keywords partition]
+    NK --> RK[13 ranking]
+    RK --> AU[14 audit snapshot optional]
+    AU --> OUT[BankTransactionResult]
+```
+
+Phases 5 and 6 run in parallel on hinted credits; phase 7 merges by transaction-id overlap.
+
+---
+
+## Business logic algorithm
+
+`SalaryTransactionExtractorService.detect()` executes these steps in order:
+
+1. **Initialise** — Load `AppConfig` (salary YAML overrides via `SalaryConfig`), `WorkingDayCalendar`, and `AuditBuilder`. Set log context from `analysis_id`.
+2. **Validate** — `run_validate_bank_transaction_payload`. Early exit on empty/invalid payload.
+3. **Normalise** — `run_normalize_bank_transactions` (credit-only filter, description cleanup).
+4. **Extract features** — `run_extract_bank_transaction_features` with salary description signals from `salary_keywords.yaml` / `negative_keywords.yaml`.
+5. **Apply hints** — `run_apply_bank_transaction_hints` for payslip anchor and approx-salary band.
+6. **Skeleton candidates** — `run_emit_skeleton_candidates` (monthly cadence groups).
+7. **Graph candidates** — `run_graph_clustering` (similarity clusters).
+8. **Dedup pool** — `run_dedup_candidate_pool` at `dedup_txn_id_overlap_pct` (default 0.90).
+9. **Bonus/expense split** — `run_bonus_expense_split` separates bonus spikes from base salary streams.
+10. **Amount/date fallback** — `run_amount_date_fallback` on unaccounted credits; emits `no_signal_detected` warning when skeleton+graph both empty.
+11. **Score** — `run_score_candidate_pool` with salary/employer hints, region inference, gap periods.
+12. **Employment transition** — `run_link_employment_transitions` merges job-change pairs (Design §15).
+13. **Negative keywords** — `partition_by_negative_keywords` moves DWP/refund/rent/etc. matches to near-misses.
+14. **Rank and return** — `run_rank_candidates` applies threshold, cap, and near-miss limits; attach audit snapshot if requested.
+
+Thread safety: services are constructed per request (or with immutable config). Do not share `WorkingDayCalendar` instances across threads.
+
+---
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+Salary uses the **core composite scoring path** (`run_score_candidate_pool`), not a business-layer YAML weights file. Weights come from core `scoring_config.yaml`, merged with salary keyword YAML via `SalaryConfig.salary_config_overrides_for_app_config()`.
+
+### Core composite weights (salary path)
+
+| Component | Weight | Source |
+|-----------|--------|--------|
+| `date_pattern_score` | 0.30 | Core `scoring_config.yaml` |
+| `description_similarity_score` | 0.25 | Core |
+| `amount_consistency_score` | 0.20 | Core |
+| `payment_channel_score` | 0.10 | Core |
+| `coverage_score` | 0.10 | Core |
+| `context_bonus` | 0.05 | Core |
+
+### Post-scoring adjustments
+
+| Stage | Effect |
+|-------|--------|
+| Employment transition | `confidence = min(cand_a, cand_b)` on merged pair |
+| Negative keywords | Candidate moved to near-miss with `near_miss_reason=negative_keyword_match` |
+| Ranking | Threshold filter only — no rescoring |
+
+### Confidence bands
+
+Applied in core scoring via `confidence_band()`: `very_high` ≥ 0.92, `high` ≥ 0.85, `medium_high` ≥ 0.70, `medium` ≥ 0.55, `low` ≥ 0.40. Default `return_threshold` = 0.40.
+
+### Further reading
+
+- Composite formula and accumulator: [`pipeline/scoring/README.md`](../../../../core/bank-transactions/src/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/scoring/README.md)
+- Hint grouping (not used by salary): [`pipeline/hint_grouping/README.md`](../../../../core/bank-transactions/src/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/hint_grouping/README.md)
+- Employment transition merge: [`pipeline/employment_transition/README.md`](../../../../core/bank-transactions/src/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/employment_transition/README.md)
+
