+
+## High-level design (HLD)
+
+### Purpose
+
+Transform raw bank-transaction rows into ranked salary candidate sets using a deterministic, multi-phase pipeline. Phases are exposed so callers can:
+
+- invoke a **single phase** over HTTP or via the tools registry (debugging, partial replay, A/B on one step), or
+- compose all phases in order (done by `salary-extractor` or custom orchestrators).
+
+### System context
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TB
+    subgraph consumers [Consumers]
+        SAL[salary-extractor business agent]
+        REST[REST clients / Postman]
+        TOOLS[LLM / MCP tool callers]
+    end
+
+    subgraph core [nw-agcore-bank-transactions]
+        CH[channels layer]
+        subgraph pipeline [pipeline phases]
+            P1[validation → ranking]
+        end
+        CH --> pipeline
+    end
+
+    subgraph libs [Shared libraries]
+        AGLIB[nw-aglib-toolkit]
+        CORE[nw-core]
+    end
+
+    SAL -->|imports run_* functions| pipeline
+    REST -->|POST /api/v1/...| CH
+    TOOLS -->|tool schemas| CH
+    core --> AGLIB
+    AGLIB --> CORE
+```
+
+### Design principles
+
+| Principle | Implementation |
+|-----------|----------------|
+| **Phase isolation** | Each phase = Tool + Service + Models + YAML config + optional REST adapter |
+| **Stateless REST** | Per-request `RouteContext` (config, calendar, region) — no shared mutable state across HTTP calls |
+| **Deterministic core** | Services are pure given inputs + merged `AppConfig` |
+| **Channel toggles** | `config/deployment.yaml` enables REST, tools, gRPC, MQ independently |
+| **Audit optional** | `AuditBuilder` passed through phases when callers request trace snapshots |
+
+### Channels (configured)
+
+From [`config/deployment.yaml`](config/deployment.yaml):
+
+| Channel | Enabled | Notes |
+|---------|---------|-------|
+| **REST** | ✅ `true` | FastAPI app, prefix `""` at mount → routes at `/api/v1/...` |
+| **Tools** | ✅ `true` | 13 `@tool` functions auto-discovered from `channels/tools/**/*Tools.py` |
+| **gRPC** | ❌ `false` | Stub servicer present; wire after codegen |
+| **MQ** | ❌ `false` | Stub handler present; not registered |
+
