+
+## Execution sequence (full pipeline)
+
+When all phases run in order (as in `SalaryTransactionExtractorService.detect`):
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[Raw payload] --> V[1 validate]
+    V -->|early exit| OUT0[Empty result + warnings]
+    V --> N[2 normalize]
+    N --> F[3 feature extraction]
+    F --> H[4 apply hints]
+    H --> S[5 skeleton candidates]
+    H --> G[6 graph clustering]
+    S --> D[7 dedup pool]
+    G --> D
+    D --> B[8 bonus/expense split]
+    B --> A[9 amount-date fallback]
+    A --> SC[10 score pool]
+    SC --> ET[11 employment transitions]
+    ET --> R[12 rank]
+    R --> OUT[Returned + near-miss candidates]
+```
+
+**Step-by-step data flow:**
+
+1. **Validate** — JSON schema + row rules; may **early-exit** with warnings only.
+2. **Normalize** — description cleanup → canonical `BankTransaction` rows.
+3. **Feature extraction** — payment channel, salary keywords, calendar features, employer tokens.
+4. **Hints** — payslip anchors, salary bands, employer hints applied to rows.
+5. **Skeleton grouping** — amount/date/description edge candidates.
+6. **Graph clustering** — similarity-graph candidates (parallel path to skeleton).
+7. **Dedup** — merge skeleton + graph pools by transaction-id overlap (`dedup_txn_id_overlap_pct` from config).
+8. **Bonus/expense split** — peel bonus/expense credits from mixed sets.
+9. **Amount-date fallback** — for **unaccounted** credits only; amount + cadence heuristics without description signal.
+10. **Scoring** — confidence, candidate type, reasoning, region inference, gap detection.
+11. **Employment transition** — link consecutive streams from different employers.
+12. **Ranking** — sort by confidence; apply return threshold and caps → **returned** vs **near-miss** sets.
+
+Optional **audit snapshot** (step 14 in business orchestrator) uses `AuditBuilder` across phases — not a separate tool in this agent.
