+# Recurrence Service (Payday Models)
+
+Shared **payday / cadence fitting** for bank-transaction clustering. Invoked by skeleton
+grouping, graph clustering, amount-date fallback, and scoring to produce a `RecurrenceFit` —
+the best-matching `PaydayModel` plus fit score, coverage, and per-month audit details.
+
+Implements Design §7.2.
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Pipeline position](#pipeline-position)
+- [Entry point](#entry-point)
+- [PaydayModel catalogue](#paydaymodel-catalogue)
+- [RecurrenceFit output](#recurrencefit-output)
+- [Model fitting algorithm](#model-fitting-algorithm)
+- [Confidence scoring formulas](#confidence-scoring-formulas)
+- [Model selection tie-breaks](#model-selection-tie-breaks)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Warnings and edge cases](#warnings-and-edge-cases)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Sequence diagram](#sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+
+## Pipeline position
+
+| Consumer phase | Usage |
+|---|---|
+| `skeleton_grouping/` | Plausibility date-pattern component |
+| `graph_clustering/` | Edge weight / cluster coherence |
+| `amount_date_fallback/` | Cadence gate (`fit_score ≥ 0.60`) |
+| `scoring/` | `date_pattern_score` and `coverage_score` inputs |
+| `ScoringPostProcess.infer_regions` | Per-region refit for UK calendar |
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    CLUSTER[BankTransaction cluster] --> FIT[fit_best_recurrence_model]
+    FIT --> MONTHLY[Monthly payday models]
+    FIT --> PERIODIC[Weekly / fortnightly / 4-weekly]
+    FIT --> IRREG[Irregular fallback]
+    MONTHLY --> BEST[Best RecurrenceFit]
+    PERIODIC --> BEST
+    IRREG --> BEST
+    BEST --> SCORE[ScoringService date_pattern_score]
+```
+
+## Entry point
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline._services.recurrence import (
+    PaydayModel,
+    RecurrenceFit,
+    fit_best_recurrence_model,
+)
+
+fit = fit_best_recurrence_model(
+    cluster,
+    calendar=working_day_calendar,
+    region="EnglandAndWales",
+)
+# fit.model, fit.fit_score, fit.coverage, fit.monthly_details
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Service | `RecurrenceService.py` | `fit_best_recurrence_model`, model-specific fitters |
+| Models | `models/PaydayModel.py` | Enum of payday regimes |
+| Models | `models/RecurrenceFit.py` | Fit result DTO |
+| Models | `models/MonthFitDetail.py` | Per-month predicted vs actual |
+
+## PaydayModel catalogue
+
+`PaydayModel` (`StrEnum`) — all values stored in `detected_pattern.payday_model`.
+
+| Enum value | Label | Fitter |
+|---|---|---|
+| `fixed_day_n` | Fixed calendar day *N* (dominant day inferred) | `_fit_fixed_day` |
+| `previous_working_day_of_n` | Previous working day before day *N* | `_fit_prev_working_day_of_n` |
+| `next_working_day_of_n` | Next working day after day *N* | `_fit_next_working_day_of_n` |
+| `nearest_working_day_of_n` | Nearest working day to day *N* | `_fit_nearest_working_day_of_n` |
+| `last_calendar_day` | Last calendar day of month | `_fit_last_calendar_day` |
+| `last_working_day` | Last **working** day of month | `_fit_last_working_day` |
+| `first_working_day` | First working day of month | `_fit_first_working_day` |
+| `weekly_same_weekday` | Every 7 days, same weekday | `_fit_periodic(7)` |
+| `fortnightly_same_weekday` | Every 14 days | `_fit_periodic(14)` |
+| `four_weekly` | Every 28 days | `_fit_periodic(28)` |
+| `irregular_salary_like` | No clean model; weak fallback | `_fit_irregular` |
+
+Fixed-day models use `_infer_fixed_day` — mode of `transaction.date.day` across cluster.
+
+Frequency labels mapped in scoring (`ScoringService._frequency_for`):
+
+| Model family | `frequency` string |
+|---|---|
+| Weekly periodic | `weekly` |
+| Fortnightly | `fortnightly` |
+| Four-weekly | `four_weekly` |
+| Irregular | `irregular` |
+| Monthly models | `monthly` |
+
+## RecurrenceFit output
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class RecurrenceFit:
+    model: PaydayModel
+    fit_score: float              # 0–1 composite
+    coverage: float               # matched / expected periods
+    mean_deviation_days: float
+    matched_count: int
+    expected_count: int
+    monthly_details: tuple[MonthFitDetail, ...] = ()
+    period_days: int | None = None   # periodic models only
+    weekday: int | None = None       # 0=Mon … 6=Sun
+    parameter_n: int | None = None   # fixed-day N
+```
+
+### `MonthFitDetail`
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `year`, `month` | Calendar month in span |
+| `predicted` | Model-predicted payday date |
+| `actual` | Closest actual credit in month (if any) |
+| `deviation_days` | Absolute day delta |
+| `explained_by_calendar` | Holiday/weekend shift absorbed |
+
+## Model fitting algorithm
+
+`fit_best_recurrence_model(cluster, calendar, region)`:
+
+1. If `len(cluster) < 2` → empty fit for `IRREGULAR_SALARY_LIKE`.
+2. Build candidate list:
+   - All monthly models (last calendar/working, first working, fixed N + working-day variants).
+   - Periodic: 7, 14, 28 day periods.
+   - Irregular fallback.
+3. Sort candidates by `(fit_score, specificity(model), matched_count)` descending.
+4. Return first (best) candidate.
+
+### Monthly fit (`_fit_monthly_model`)
+
+Span: first to last transaction date. Expected months = inclusive month range.
+
+For each month:
+
+- Predict payday via model-specific `predict(y, m)`.
+- Match closest actual credit in that month.
+- `effective_deviation = 0` if calendar explains shift, else `|actual - predicted|`.
+
+Aggregates:
+
+\[
+\text{mean\_deviation} = \text{avg}(\text{effective\_deviations})
+\]
+
+\[
+\text{date\_fit} = \max\left(0,\; 1 - \frac{\text{mean\_deviation}}{D_{\max}}\right)
+\]
+
+where \(D_{\max} = 7\) (`_MAX_DEVIATION_DAYS`).
+
+\[
+\text{coverage} = \frac{\text{matched\_count}}{\text{expected\_count}}
+\]
+
+\[
+\boxed{\text{fit\_score} = 0.60 \times \text{date\_fit} + 0.40 \times \text{coverage}}
+\]
+
+### Periodic fit (`_fit_periodic`)
+
+Gap analysis between sorted credits:
+
+\[
+\text{mean\_gap\_dev} = \text{avg}(| \text{gap}_i - \text{period\_days} |)
+\]
+
+\[
+\text{gap\_fit} = \begin{cases}
+1.0 & \text{if mean\_gap\_dev} \leq 2 \\
+\max\left(0,\; 1 - \dfrac{\text{mean\_gap\_dev} - 2}{\text{period\_days}}\right) & \text{otherwise}
+\end{cases}
+\]
+
+\[
+\text{weekday\_consistency} = \frac{\text{count of dominant weekday}}{\text{len(cluster)}}
+\]
+
+\[
+\text{expected\_count} = \max\left(1,\; \left\lfloor \dfrac{\text{span\_days}}{\text{period\_days}} \right\rfloor + 1\right)
+\]
+
+\[
+\text{coverage} = \min\left(1,\; \dfrac{\text{len(cluster)}}{\text{expected\_count}}\right)
+\]
+
+\[
+\boxed{\text{fit\_score} = 0.55 \times \text{gap\_fit} + 0.25 \times \text{weekday\_consistency} + 0.20 \times \text{coverage}}
+\]
+
+### Irregular fit (`_fit_irregular`)
+
+Requires ≥ 3 transactions:
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `fit_score` | 0.30 |
+| `coverage` | 1.0 |
+| `matched_count` | len(cluster) |
+
+## Confidence scoring formulas
+
+Recurrence output feeds scoring **indirectly**:
+
+| Downstream use | Field |
+|---|---|
+| `ScoreBreakdown.date_pattern_score` | `fit_score` |
+| `ScoreBreakdown.coverage_score` | `coverage` |
+| Amount-date fallback gate | `fit_score ≥ 0.60` |
+| Amount-date fallback confidence bump | `0.40 + 0.10 × fit_score` |
+| Region inference | Compare monthly model `fit_score` per UK region |
+
+This module does **not** assign candidate-level `confidence` or `confidence_details`.
+
+## Model selection tie-breaks
+
+When `fit_score` ties, `_specificity(model)` prefers more structured models:
+
+| Model | Specificity rank |
+|---|---|
+| `LAST_WORKING_DAY`, `FIRST_WORKING_DAY` | 10 |
+| `PREVIOUS/NEXT/NEAREST_WORKING_DAY_OF_N` | 9 |
+| `WEEKLY/FORTNIGHTLY/FOUR_WEEKLY` | 8 |
+| `LAST_CALENDAR_DAY` | 6 |
+| `FIXED_DAY_N` | 5 |
+| `IRREGULAR_SALARY_LIKE` | 0 |
+
+Third tie-break: higher `matched_count`.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Location |
+|---|---|---|
+| `_MAX_DEVIATION_DAYS` | `7` | `RecurrenceService.py` |
+| `_DEFAULT_REGION` | `EnglandAndWales` | same |
+| Periodic gap slack | `2` days | `_fit_periodic` |
+| Monthly score weights | 0.60 / 0.40 | `_fit_monthly_model` |
+| Periodic score weights | 0.55 / 0.25 / 0.20 | `_fit_periodic` |
+
+UK bank holidays and working-day rules come from `nw_core.calendar.WorkingDayCalendar` and
+`pipeline/calendar/config/` YAML — not from this package.
+
+Region parameter affects **working-day** monthly models only; passed through from callers
+(e.g. amount-date fallback, region inference).
+
+## Warnings and edge cases
+
+| Situation | Behaviour |
+|---|---|
+| &lt; 2 transactions | Empty fit, score 0 |
+| &lt; 3 transactions for irregular | Empty irregular fit |
+| Month with no credit | `actual=None` in `MonthFitDetail`, lowers coverage |
+| `predicted is None` | Month skipped in match count |
+| Scotland / NI holidays | Different `last_working_day` via `region` |
+
+No `ValidationWarning` codes originate here. Ambiguous region warnings are emitted by
+`ScoringPostProcess.infer_regions` after refitting per region.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[cluster ≥ 2 txns] --> INF[_infer_fixed_day optional N]
+    INF --> CANDS[Build candidate RecurrenceFit list]
+    CANDS --> M1[last calendar / working / first working]
+    CANDS --> M2[fixed N + working-day variants]
+    CANDS --> P[weekly / fortnightly / four-weekly]
+    CANDS --> I[irregular]
+    M1 --> MONTH[_fit_monthly_model per candidate]
+    M2 --> MONTH
+    MONTH --> SCORE_M[fit_score = 0.6×date_fit + 0.4×coverage]
+    P --> PER[_fit_periodic]
+    PER --> SCORE_P[fit_score = 0.55×gap + 0.25×weekday + 0.20×cov]
+    I --> SCORE_I[fit_score = 0.30]
+    SCORE_M --> SORT[Sort by fit_score, specificity, matched_count]
+    SCORE_P --> SORT
+    SCORE_I --> SORT
+    SORT --> OUT[Best RecurrenceFit]
+```
+
+## Sequence diagram
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    participant Scoring as ScoringService.compute_score
+    participant Rec as RecurrenceService
+    participant Cal as WorkingDayCalendar
+
+    Scoring->>Rec: fit_best_recurrence_model(cluster, calendar, region)
+    loop each candidate model
+        Rec->>Cal: last_working_day / next_working_day / …
+        Cal-->>Rec: predicted dates
+        Rec->>Rec: _fit_monthly_model or _fit_periodic
+    end
+    Rec-->>Scoring: RecurrenceFit (best)
+    Note over Scoring: date_pattern_score = fit.fit_score
+```
