+# Amount / Date Fallback (Phase 13 candidate generation)
+
+Final candidate-generation path for credits that earlier phases miss. Skeleton grouping (phase 5)
+and graph clustering (phase 7) require shared description tokens or character patterns. When
+salary streams use opaque descriptions (e.g. per-payment UUIDs) but exhibit stable amounts and
+monthly cadence, this module emits low-confidence `unknown_recurring_credit` candidates tagged
+`metadata.source = "amount_date_fallback"`.
+
+Triggered fixture: `realistic_10_uuid_clean_cadence`. Correctly **does not** trigger on
+`realistic_11_uuid_no_signal` (random amounts and dates fail cadence).
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Pipeline position](#pipeline-position)
+- [Entry points](#entry-points)
+- [Inputs and outputs](#inputs-and-outputs)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Warnings and edge cases](#warnings-and-edge-cases)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Sequence diagram](#sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+
+## Pipeline position
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Phase number | 13 (generation); rescored in phase 11 |
+| Audit phase name | `amount_date_fallback` |
+| Upstream | Unaccounted credits after skeleton/graph/dedup assignment |
+| Downstream | Merged into pool → `run_score_candidate_pool` (cap enforced again in scoring) |
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    UNACCT[Unaccounted credits] --> FB[run_amount_date_fallback]
+    FB --> BUCKET[Amount band buckets]
+    BUCKET --> CADENCE[fit_best_recurrence_model]
+    CADENCE --> EMIT[CandidateSet per bucket]
+    EMIT --> POOL[Merged candidate pool]
+    POOL --> SCORE[Phase 11 scoring with 0.55 cap]
+```
+
+## Entry points
+
+### Tool
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.amount_date_fallback import (
+    run_amount_date_fallback,
+)
+
+result = run_amount_date_fallback(
+    unaccounted,
+    calendar,
+    features_by_id,
+    config=config,
+    applied_hints=applied_hints,
+    region="EnglandAndWales",
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+candidates = list(result.candidates)
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Tool | `AmountDateFallbackTools.py` | `run_amount_date_fallback` via `CustomTool` wrapper |
+| Service | `AmountDateFallbackService.py` | `emit_candidates` — bucketing + cadence filter |
+| Models | `models/AmountDateFallbackToolResult.py` | `candidates`, inherited `warnings` |
+| REST | `routes/AmountDateFallbackRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapter |
+
+### REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/scoring/amount-date-fallback` |
+| OpenAPI | `routes/openapi/run_amount_date_fallback.openapi.yaml` |
+
+### Sample request
+
+```json
+{"unaccounted": [], "features_by_id": {}}
+```
+
+### Sample response
+
+```json
+{"candidates": [], "warnings": []}
+```
+
+## Inputs and outputs
+
+### Input
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `unaccounted` | `Sequence[BankTransaction]` | yes | Credit rows not in any prior candidate |
+| `calendar` | `WorkingDayCalendar` | yes | UK working-day calendar for recurrence fit |
+| `features_by_id` | `dict[str, TransactionFeatures]` | yes | Anchor detection via `group_has_anchor` |
+| `config` | `AppConfig` | yes | Amount band tolerance from `amount_config()` |
+| `applied_hints` | `AppliedHints \| None` | no | Payslip anchors |
+| `region` | `str` | no | Default `EnglandAndWales` |
+
+Early exit: fewer than `_MIN_CREDITS_PER_BUCKET` (4) unaccounted credits → empty tuple.
+
+### Output candidate shape
+
+Each emitted `CandidateSet` includes:
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `candidate_set_id` | `amount_date_{idx:03d}` |
+| `candidate_type` | `unknown_recurring_credit` |
+| `metadata.source` | `"amount_date_fallback"` |
+| `metadata.amount_date_only` | `true` |
+| `metadata.fallback_confidence_cap` | `0.55` (default) |
+| `metadata.anchor_in_cluster` | bool from anchor resolution |
+| `reasoning` | Cadence + amount-band narrative |
+| `risks` | No employer / payroll signal warning |
+
+## Business logic
+
+`AmountDateFallbackService.emit_candidates`:
+
+1. **Amount bucketing** (`_bucket_by_amount`) — greedy single pass:
+   - Sort credits by amount ascending.
+   - Place each credit in the first bucket whose median is within `±band_tolerance` relative
+     difference; otherwise start a new bucket.
+   - Sort each bucket by date for determinism.
+2. **Per-bucket filters**:
+   - Skip buckets with fewer than `_min_credits` (4) members.
+   - `fit = fit_best_recurrence_model(members, calendar, region)`.
+   - Skip when `fit.fit_score < _min_cadence_fit` (0.60).
+3. **Build candidate** (`_build_candidate`):
+   - `DetectedPattern` from recurrence model and amount stability (CV ≤ 0.02 → `stable`).
+   - `ScoreBreakdown` with date, amount consistency, and coverage sub-scores.
+   - Confidence from formula below (capped).
+
+### Amount band rule
+
+For median `M` and tolerance `τ` (default 0.10):
+
+\[
+\text{in\_band}(a) \iff \frac{|a - M|}{M} \leq \tau
+\]
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+### Interim confidence (this phase)
+
+\[
+\text{confidence} = \min\left(
+  \text{cap},\;
+  0.40 + 0.10 \times \text{fit\_score} + \begin{cases} 0.05 & \text{if anchor present} \\ 0 & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}
+\right)
+\]
+
+Rounded to 4 decimal places. Default `cap = 0.55`.
+
+| Sub-score | Formula |
+|---|---|
+| `date_pattern_score` | `fit.fit_score` |
+| `amount_consistency_score` | `1.0` if CV ≤ 0.02 else `max(0, 1 - 5 × CV)` |
+| `coverage_score` | `fit.coverage` |
+
+### Confidence bands (local helper `_band_for_score`)
+
+| Band | Threshold |
+|---|---|
+| `high` | ≥ 0.85 |
+| `medium_high` | ≥ 0.70 |
+| `medium` | ≥ 0.55 |
+| `low` | ≥ 0.40 |
+| `very_low` | &lt; 0.40 |
+
+With the 0.55 cap, emitted candidates typically land in `medium` or below.
+
+### Phase 11 re-score guard
+
+`ScoringService.score_candidate` detects `metadata.source == "amount_date_fallback"` and:
+
+- clamps `final_score` at `metadata.fallback_confidence_cap` (default 0.55), and
+- forces `candidate_type = unknown_recurring_credit` (prevents promotion to `probable_salary` on
+  clean recurrence fit alone).
+
+This phase does **not** populate `confidence_details`; audit trail is added during scoring when
+the candidate is rescored.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Source | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `_BAND_TOLERANCE_PCT` | `0.10` | `AmountDateFallbackService.py` | Overridden by `config.amount_config().moderate_pct_tolerance` |
+| `_MIN_CADENCE_FIT` | `0.60` | module constant | Recurrence `fit_score` floor |
+| `_MIN_CREDITS_PER_BUCKET` | `4` | module constant | Minimum credits per bucket |
+| `_CONFIDENCE_CAP` | `0.55` | module constant | Hard confidence ceiling |
+| `amount.moderate_pct_tolerance` | `0.10` | `scoring/config/amount_config.yaml` | Band half-width |
+
+No dedicated YAML file under `amount_date_fallback/config/` — thresholds are service constants
+with one merge from `amount_config`.
+
+## Warnings and edge cases
+
+| Situation | Behaviour |
+|---|---|
+| &lt; 4 unaccounted credits | No candidates emitted |
+| Bucket fails cadence fit | Bucket skipped silently |
+| Zero median in bucket | Credit skipped during band placement |
+| Anchor in cluster | +0.05 confidence bump (still capped at 0.55) |
+| Random UUID + clean cadence | Expected trigger (`realistic_10`) |
+| Random amounts + dates | No emission (`realistic_11`) |
+
+This phase does not append `ValidationWarning` entries. Downstream scoring may emit
+`missing_salary_periods` via `ScoringPostProcess.apply_gap_periods`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[unaccounted credits] --> MIN{count ≥ 4?}
+    MIN -- no --> EMPTY[return empty]
+    MIN -- yes --> BUCKET[_bucket_by_amount]
+    BUCKET --> LOOP[For each bucket]
+    LOOP --> SIZE{bucket size ≥ 4?}
+    SIZE -- no --> SKIP1[next bucket]
+    SIZE -- yes --> FIT[fit_best_recurrence_model]
+    FIT --> CAD{fit_score ≥ 0.60?}
+    CAD -- no --> SKIP2[next bucket]
+    CAD -- yes --> BUILD[_build_candidate]
+    BUILD --> ANCHOR[group_has_anchor?]
+    ANCHOR --> CONF[confidence = min cap, 0.40 + 0.10×fit + anchor bump]
+    CONF --> EMIT[CandidateSet amount_date_NNN]
+    EMIT --> OUT[AmountDateFallbackToolResult]
+    SKIP1 --> LOOP
+    SKIP2 --> LOOP
+```
+
+## Sequence diagram
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    participant Client
+    participant Route as AmountDateFallbackRoute
+    participant Tool as AmountDateFallbackTools
+    participant Svc as AmountDateFallbackService
+    participant Rec as RecurrenceService
+
+    Client->>Route: POST /scoring/amount-date-fallback
+    Route->>Tool: run_amount_date_fallback(...)
+    Tool->>Svc: emit_candidates(unaccounted, calendar, ...)
+    loop each amount bucket
+        Svc->>Rec: fit_best_recurrence_model(members)
+        Rec-->>Svc: RecurrenceFit
+        Svc->>Svc: _build_candidate (confidence cap)
+    end
+    Svc-->>Tool: tuple[CandidateSet, ...]
+    Tool-->>Route: AmountDateFallbackToolResult
+    Route-->>Client: JSON candidates
+```
+
+## Key source files
+
+| File | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `AmountDateFallbackService.py` | Bucketing, cadence gate, candidate builder |
+| `AmountDateFallbackTools.py` | Public tool, TRACE `fallback.candidate` logs |
+| `models/AmountDateFallbackToolResult.py` | Result DTO |
+| `routes/AmountDateFallbackRoute.py` | REST adapter |
+
+Shared recurrence logic: `pipeline/_services/recurrence/RecurrenceService.py`.
+
+## Tests
+
+| Test | Location | Coverage |
+|---|---|---|
+| REST smoke | `tests/feature/.../amount_date_fallback/test_rest.py` | Endpoint returns candidates |
+| Fixture | `tests/fixtures/scenarios/realistic/realistic_10_uuid_clean_cadence.yaml` | Positive trigger |
+| Fixture | `tests/fixtures/scenarios/realistic/realistic_11_uuid_no_signal.yaml` | Negative control |
+
+Unit tests for bucketing and confidence formula are planned (`AmountDateFallbackTest.py`).
+
+## Related modules
+
+- **`_services/recurrence/`** — `fit_best_recurrence_model` for cadence scoring.
+- **`scoring/`** — rescored with cap enforcement; see `score_candidate` fallback branch.
+- **`hints/AnchorResolution.py`** — `group_has_anchor`, `use_anchor_enriched_features`.
+- **Phase 5/7** — primary paths that must fail before fallback applies.
+
+## Thread safety
+
+`AmountDateFallbackService` is constructed per request with `AppConfig`. Do not share
+`WorkingDayCalendar` instances across threads.
+
+## TRACE logging
+
+The `@tool` wrapper logs request JSON at TRACE. Each emitted candidate logs
+`fallback.candidate id=… txns=N`.
