+# Bonus and Expense Split (Phase 9)
+
+Splits bonus and expense-reimbursement credits out of mixed salary-like candidate sets
+**before** final scoring. Implements Design §15.5. Downstream phase 11 (`scoring/`) classifies
+sub-candidates by amount model; phase 12 (`employment_transition/`) renames split ids to
+`bonus_or_extra_pay_candidate` / `expense_reimbursement_candidate`.
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Pipeline position](#pipeline-position)
+- [Entry points](#entry-points)
+- [Inputs and outputs](#inputs-and-outputs)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Warnings and edge cases](#warnings-and-edge-cases)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Sequence diagram](#sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+
+## Pipeline position
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Phase number | 9 |
+| Audit phase name | `bonus_expense_split` |
+| Upstream | Phase 5/7 candidate pools (skeleton / graph clustering) merged and deduped |
+| Downstream | Phase 11 `run_score_candidate_pool` → Phase 12 `run_link_employment_transitions` |
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    POOL[Candidate pool from phases 5/7] --> SPLIT[run_bonus_expense_split]
+    SPLIT --> MAIN[main sub-candidates]
+    SPLIT --> FLAGGED[bonus / expense sub-candidates]
+    MAIN --> SCORE[Phase 11 scoring]
+    FLAGGED --> SCORE
+    SCORE --> ET[Phase 12 employment_transition type override]
+```
+
+## Entry points
+
+### Tool
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.bonus_expense_split import (
+    run_bonus_expense_split,
+)
+
+result = run_bonus_expense_split(pool, normalised, audit=audit, warnings=warnings)
+candidates = list(result.candidates)
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Tool | `BonusExpenseSplitTools.py` | `run_bonus_expense_split` via `CustomTool` logging/audit wrapper |
+| Service | `BonusExpenseSplitService.py` | `split_bonus_and_expense_credits` — deterministic split logic |
+| Models | `models/BonusExpenseSplitToolResult.py` | `candidates`, inherited `warnings` |
+| REST | `routes/BonusExpenseSplitRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapter |
+
+### REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/scoring/bonus-expense-split` |
+| OpenAPI | `routes/openapi/run_bonus_expense_split.openapi.yaml` |
+
+### Sample request (`result` field)
+
+```json
+{"pool": [], "normalised": []}
+```
+
+### Sample response
+
+```json
+{"candidates": [], "warnings": []}
+```
+
+## Inputs and outputs
+
+### Input
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `pool` | `Sequence[CandidateSet]` | yes | Placeholder candidates from generation phases |
+| `normalised` | `Iterable[BankTransaction]` | yes | Lookup for `description_tokens` per transaction id |
+
+Only `candidate_set_id`, `transactions`, and transaction ids are mutated. Score fields are
+carried through unchanged on both sub-candidates.
+
+### Output: `BonusExpenseSplitToolResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class BonusExpenseSplitToolResult(BaseToolModel):
+    candidates: tuple[CandidateSet, ...] = ()
+```
+
+When a split occurs, one input candidate becomes **two** outputs:
+
+| Sub-candidate | Id suffix | Typical downstream type (phase 11) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Main salary stream | `{id}_main` | `probable_salary` / `possible_salary` |
+| Bonus credits | `{id}_bonus_{NN}` | `bonus_or_extra_pay_candidate` |
+| Expense credits | `{id}_expense_{NN}` | `expense_reimbursement_candidate` |
+
+`{NN}` is a zero-padded split index (`00`, `01`, …) incremented per split in the pool.
+
+## Business logic
+
+`BonusExpenseSplitService.split_bonus_and_expense_credits` iterates each candidate in `pool`:
+
+1. **Partition transactions** by description tokens on the matching `BankTransaction`:
+   - **Flagged** — token set intersects `_BONUS_TOKENS` (`BONUS`) or `_EXPENSE_TOKENS`
+     (`EXPENSES`, `EXPENSE`, `REIMBURSEMENT`).
+   - **Normal** — all other transactions (including rows missing from `normalised` lookup).
+2. **Split gate** — split only when **both**:
+   - at least one flagged transaction exists, and
+   - the normal subset has **≥ 2** transactions (a lone normal credit stays unsplit).
+3. **Expense vs bonus suffix** — if any flagged row matches `_EXPENSE_TOKENS`, sub-id uses
+   `expense`; otherwise `bonus`.
+4. **Emit** — `dataclasses.replace` on the original candidate with new id and transaction tuple
+   for each sub-candidate; append both to output. Unsplit candidates pass through unchanged.
+
+### Token constants
+
+| Constant | Tokens |
+|---|---|
+| `_BONUS_TOKENS` | `BONUS` |
+| `_EXPENSE_TOKENS` | `EXPENSES`, `EXPENSE`, `REIMBURSEMENT` |
+
+Token matching is exact set intersection on normalised `description_tokens` (Phase 2 output).
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+This phase **does not compute confidence**. Sub-candidates inherit the parent candidate's
+empty or interim scores. Canonical confidence is assigned in phase 11:
+
+- Main stream — full composite score via `ScoringService.score_candidate`.
+- Flagged stream — amount-model branch in `CandidateType.classify_candidate_type` may emit
+  `bonus_or_extra_pay_candidate` or `expense_reimbursement_candidate` based on outlier /
+  variability heuristics.
+
+Phase 12 `override_split_subcandidate_types` forces the final `candidate_type` for ids
+containing `_bonus_` or `_expense_` regardless of generic classification.
+
+## Configuration
+
+No dedicated YAML section. Token sets are module constants in `BonusExpenseSplitService.py`.
+Tune by editing `_BONUS_TOKENS` / `_EXPENSE_TOKENS` and updating tests.
+
+| Key | Default | Location |
+|---|---|---|
+| `_BONUS_TOKENS` | `{BONUS}` | `BonusExpenseSplitService.py` |
+| `_EXPENSE_TOKENS` | `{EXPENSES, EXPENSE, REIMBURSEMENT}` | same |
+| Min normal transactions for split | `2` | hard-coded gate |
+
+## Warnings and edge cases
+
+| Situation | Behaviour |
+|---|---|
+| Transaction id not in `normalised` | Treated as **normal** (not flagged) |
+| Only flagged rows, or normal count &lt; 2 | Candidate passes through unsplit |
+| Mixed bonus + expense tokens in one flagged set | `expense` suffix wins if any expense token present |
+| Missing description tokens | Empty token set → normal partition |
+
+This phase does **not** emit `ValidationWarning` entries. TRACE logs sub-candidate ids when
+`_main`, `_bonus_`, or `_expense_` appear in `candidate_set_id`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[pool + normalised] --> LOOP[For each CandidateSet]
+    LOOP --> LOOKUP[Build txn_by_id from normalised]
+    LOOKUP --> PART[Partition txns: flagged vs normal]
+    PART --> GATE{flagged non-empty AND normal ≥ 2?}
+    GATE -- no --> PASS[Append original candidate]
+    GATE -- yes --> SPLIT[Create main + flagged sub-candidates]
+    SPLIT --> SUFFIX{Any expense token?}
+    SUFFIX -- yes --> EXP[id suffix _expense_NN]
+    SUFFIX -- no --> BON[id suffix _bonus_NN]
+    EXP --> OUT[Append main + flagged]
+    BON --> OUT
+    PASS --> RES[BonusExpenseSplitToolResult]
+    OUT --> RES
+```
+
+## Sequence diagram
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    participant Client
+    participant Route as BonusExpenseSplitRoute
+    participant Tool as BonusExpenseSplitTools
+    participant Svc as BonusExpenseSplitService
+
+    Client->>Route: POST /scoring/bonus-expense-split
+    Route->>Route: bank_transactions_from_wire, candidate_sets_from_wire
+    Route->>Tool: run_bonus_expense_split(pool, normalised)
+    Tool->>Svc: split_bonus_and_expense_credits(pool, normalised)
+    Svc-->>Tool: tuple[CandidateSet, ...]
+    Tool-->>Route: BonusExpenseSplitToolResult
+    Route-->>Client: JSON result.candidates
+```
+
+## Key source files
+
+| File | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `BonusExpenseSplitService.py` | Split algorithm and token constants |
+| `BonusExpenseSplitTools.py` | Public tool wrapper, TRACE split logging |
+| `models/BonusExpenseSplitToolResult.py` | Result DTO |
+| `routes/BonusExpenseSplitRoute.py` | REST adapter |
+
+## Tests
+
+| Test | Location | Coverage |
+|---|---|---|
+| REST smoke | `tests/feature/.../bonus_expense_split/test_rest.py` | Endpoint returns candidate list |
+| Registry | `tests/feature/.../channels/tools/test_registry.py` | Tool registered |
+
+Unit tests for split gates and id suffixes are planned (`BonusExpenseSplitTest.py` per refactor
+plan). When changing token sets or the min-normal threshold, add fixtures with mixed
+BONUS/EXPENSE description tokens.
+
+## Related modules
+
+- **Phase 11** `scoring/` — assigns confidence and classifies amount patterns on split sets.
+- **Phase 12** `employment_transition/` — overrides `candidate_type` for `_bonus_` / `_expense_` ids.
+- **Phase 2** `normalization/` — supplies `description_tokens` used for flag detection.
+
+## Thread safety
+
+Services are instantiated per call (or use immutable config only). REST handlers build a fresh
+`RouteContext` per request.
+
+## TRACE logging
+
+The `@tool` wrapper logs linearised request JSON at TRACE level as `tool.request {...}`.
+Sub-candidate emission logs `split.sub_candidate id=… txns=N`.
