+# Employment Transition Linking
+
+**Pipeline phase:** 11 — `employment_transition`  
+**Design reference:** Design §15 / FR edge-case linking
+
+Detects consecutive salary streams from **different employers** and either merges them into one
+`probable_salary` candidate or annotates the earlier stream with transition metadata and optional
+`gap_period_candidates`.
+
+Runs **after** scoring (phase 10) so merge eligibility uses final `candidate_type` and
+`confidence` values. Output feeds phase 12 ranking (and optional negative-keyword partition in
+the salary-extractor orchestrator).
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Purpose and pipeline position](#purpose-and-pipeline-position)
+- [Entry points](#entry-points)
+- [Inputs and outputs](#inputs-and-outputs)
+- [Design](#design)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Warnings and edge cases](#warnings-and-edge-cases)
+- [Sequence diagram](#sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+
+---
+
+## Purpose and pipeline position
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    SC[10 scoring\nrun_score_candidate_pool] --> ET[11 employment_transition\nrun_link_employment_transitions]
+    ET --> NK[negative_keyword partition\nsalary-extractor only]
+    NK --> R[12 ranking\nrun_rank_candidates]
+```
+
+| Direction | Phase | Tool |
+|-----------|-------|------|
+| Upstream | 10 — scoring | `run_score_candidate_pool` |
+| This phase | 11 — employment transition | `run_link_employment_transitions` |
+| Downstream | 12 — ranking | `run_rank_candidates` |
+
+Implements employment-change linking: when a payer ends and a new employer stream starts within
+62 days, the module warns, optionally merges, or attaches low-confidence continuation credits as
+`gap_period_candidates`.
+
+---
+
+## Entry points
+
+### Tool (primary)
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.employment_transition import (
+    run_link_employment_transitions,
+)
+
+result = run_link_employment_transitions(scored, config, audit=audit, warnings=warnings)
+linked = list(result.scored)
+# result.warnings → employment_transition_detected ValidationWarnings
+```
+
+Lazy import path (same function):
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.employment_transition.EmploymentTransitionTools import (
+    run_link_employment_transitions,
+)
+```
+
+### Service (direct logic)
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.employment_transition.EmploymentTransitionService import (
+    link_employment_transitions,
+    merge_transition_pair,
+    override_split_subcandidate_types,
+    same_employer,
+)
+
+linked, extra_warnings = link_employment_transitions(scored, config)
+linked = override_split_subcandidate_types(linked)
+```
+
+### REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Tool | `run_link_employment_transitions` |
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/scoring/employment-transition` |
+| Route | `channels/rest/routes/EmploymentTransitionRoute.py` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/routes/openapi/run_link_employment_transitions.openapi.yaml` |
+
+Audit phase name: `employment_transition`.
+
+### Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|-------|---------|
+| INFO | Phase start/done via `EmploymentTransitionTools` (`phase=employment_transition`) |
+| DEBUG | Every pair evaluation: ids, types, confidences, spans, gap, merge/skip reason |
+| TRACE | Each `employment_transition_detected` warning detail (via tool wrapper) |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.employment_transition.EmploymentTransitionTools`.
+
+Services are stateless and instantiated per call. REST handlers build a fresh `RouteContext` per
+request — do not share mutable state across threads.
+
+---
+
+## Inputs and outputs
+
+### Input: `CandidateSet`
+
+Required fields used by this module:
+
+| Field | Type | Usage |
+|-------|------|-------|
+| `candidate_set_id` | `str` | Pair keys, merged id suffix `_transition` |
+| `candidate_type` | `str` | Gate on A; mergeable-type check on B |
+| `confidence` | `float` | Merge threshold gate (both ≥ 0.55) |
+| `confidence_band` | `str` | Recalculated on merge |
+| `transactions` | `tuple[CandidateTransaction, …]` | ISO dates; union on merge |
+| `detected_pattern.possible_employer_tokens` | `tuple[str, …]` | `same_employer()` overlap test |
+| `metadata` | `dict` | Transition annotations |
+| `gap_period_candidates` | `tuple[GapPeriodCandidate, …]` | Extended in low-confidence path |
+| `reasoning` | `str` | Appended on merge |
+
+Also accepts `AppConfig` (reserved for future threshold overrides; currently ignored via `del config`).
+
+### Output: `EmploymentTransitionToolResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class EmploymentTransitionToolResult(BaseToolModel):
+    scored: tuple[CandidateSet, ...] = ()
+    # warnings: inherited — employment_transition_detected entries
+    # audit: ToolAuditData when include_audit=True
+```
+
+The salary-extractor orchestrator uses `result.scored` as input to phase 12 ranking.
+
+Output list preserves non-absorbed candidates; absorbed B ids are dropped from the emitted list.
+
+---
+
+## Design
+
+Two passes execute in one tool call: `link_employment_transitions` then
+`override_split_subcandidate_types`.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[scored candidates from phase 10] --> IDX[Build indexed list: first_date, last_date, cand]
+    IDX --> LOOP[For each cand_a in indexed order]
+    LOOP --> PAIR[For each cand_b starting after cand_a]
+    PAIR --> GAP{0 ≤ gap ≤ 62?}
+    GAP -- no --> SKIP1[DEBUG skip gap_out_of_range]
+    GAP -- yes --> EMP{same_employer?}
+    EMP -- yes --> SKIP2[DEBUG skip same_employer]
+    EMP -- no --> TYPEA{cand_a type == probable_salary?}
+    TYPEA -- no --> SKIP3[DEBUG skip cand_a_not_probable_salary]
+    TYPEA -- yes --> MERGEABLE{cand_b in mergeable types?}
+    MERGEABLE -- yes --> WARN[Append employment_transition_detected warning]
+    WARN --> CONF{both conf ≥ 0.55?}
+    CONF -- yes --> MERGE[merge_transition_pair → replace cand_a]
+    CONF -- no --> GAPC[Attach gap_period_candidates + metadata]
+    MERGEABLE -- no --> META[metadata-only possible_employment_transition]
+    MERGE --> OUT[Emit merged list minus absorbed B]
+    GAPC --> OUT
+    META --> OUT
+    OUT --> OVERRIDE[override_split_subcandidate_types]
+    OVERRIDE --> RES[EmploymentTransitionToolResult]
+```
+
+---
+
+## Business logic
+
+### Pass 1 — `link_employment_transitions`
+
+For every ordered pair of candidates `(cand_a, cand_b)` where `cand_b` starts **after**
+`cand_a`:
+
+1. **Gap filter** — `0 ≤ gap_days ≤ 62` between `cand_a` last txn and `cand_b` first txn.
+2. **Employer filter** — skip if `same_employer()` (any overlap in
+   `detected_pattern.possible_employer_tokens`; empty token sets do not match).
+3. **Type gate on A** — `cand_a.candidate_type` must be `probable_salary`.
+4. **Mergeable B types** — `cand_b.candidate_type ∈ {probable_salary, final_pay_candidate, possible_salary}`.
+
+When a transition is detected (B in mergeable types):
+
+- Emit `ValidationWarning(code="employment_transition_detected", …)` once per pair.
+- If **both** confidences ≥ `0.55` → **merge** via `merge_transition_pair`; B is absorbed.
+- If B is mergeable but B confidence &lt; 0.55 → attach B's transactions as
+  `gap_period_candidates` on A; set `metadata.possible_employment_transition` with
+  `note="low_confidence_stream"`.
+- If B is not mergeable → metadata-only `possible_employment_transition` annotation.
+
+Additional metadata on A:
+
+- `same_month_overlap=True` when A's last month equals B's first month.
+- For `final_pay_candidate` A overlapping a `probable_salary` B within 31 days (same employer)
+  → `metadata.attached_to_salary_candidate`.
+
+Pair evaluation stops at the first merge for a given `cand_a` (inner loop `break` after merge).
+
+### Pass 2 — `override_split_subcandidate_types`
+
+Post-pass rename for bonus/expense **sub-candidates** created in the bonus/expense split phase:
+
+| `candidate_set_id` suffix | New `candidate_type` |
+|---------------------------|----------------------|
+| `…_bonus_…` | `bonus_or_extra_pay_candidate` |
+| `…_expense_…` | `expense_reimbursement_candidate` |
+
+Runs after linking so generic scoring classification is overridden for split ids.
+
+### Merge semantics (`merge_transition_pair`)
+
+When merge executes:
+
+- **Transactions** — union of A and B, sorted by date.
+- **Employer tokens** — set union on `detected_pattern.possible_employer_tokens`.
+- **Type** — forced to `probable_salary`.
+- **Confidence** — `min(cand_a.confidence, cand_b.confidence)` (rounded to 4 dp).
+- **Id** — `{cand_a.candidate_set_id}_transition`.
+- **Reasoning** — appended employment-transition narrative (includes B's original type when
+  `final_pay_candidate` or `possible_salary`).
+- **Metadata** — `employment_transition` block with from/to ids, gap, transition months.
+- **Audit on absorbed txns** — each B transaction gets a `ConfidenceDetail` with
+  `step="employment_transition_merge"`.
+
+---
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+This phase does **not** recompute composite scores from phase 10. It adjusts confidence only
+on merge and stamps audit details on absorbed transactions.
+
+| Scenario | Confidence behaviour |
+|----------|---------------------|
+| Merge (both ≥ 0.55) | `confidence = min(cand_a.confidence, cand_b.confidence)` |
+| Low-confidence B | B transactions copied into `gap_period_candidates` with B's confidence |
+| Metadata-only | No confidence change |
+| Post-merge band | `_confidence_band()` recalculated from merged score (same thresholds as scoring) |
+
+`ConfidenceDetail` on merge:
+
+```python
+ConfidenceDetail(
+    step="employment_transition_merge",
+    confidence_step=merged_conf,
+    confidence_step_max_value=1.0,
+    reasoning="Absorbed from … via employment-transition merge; …",
+)
+```
+
+Band thresholds (local helper, aligned with scoring):
+
+| Band | Threshold |
+|------|-----------|
+| `high` | ≥ 0.85 |
+| `medium_high` | ≥ 0.70 |
+| `medium` | ≥ 0.55 |
+| `low` | ≥ 0.40 |
+| `very_low` | &lt; 0.40 |
+
+---
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Location | Notes |
+|-----|---------|----------|-------|
+| `_TRANSITION_MERGE_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` | `0.55` | `EmploymentTransitionService.py` | Module constant; not yet exposed via YAML |
+| `_TRANSITION_MERGEABLE_TYPES` | `probable_salary`, `final_pay_candidate`, `possible_salary` | same | Frozenset of B types eligible for merge |
+| Max gap | `62` days | same | Hard-coded |
+| Same-month overlap flag | derived | same | When A last month == B first month |
+| Final-pay attach window | `31` days | same | Same-employer final_pay → probable_salary link |
+| `AppConfig` | — | `link_employment_transitions(..., config)` | Accepted; reserved for future threshold overrides |
+
+No dedicated YAML section under `pipeline/employment_transition/config/` — tune constants in
+`EmploymentTransitionService.py` and update employment-transition tests if thresholds change.
+
+---
+
+## Warnings and edge cases
+
+| Code | When emitted | Detail |
+|------|--------------|--------|
+| `employment_transition_detected` | B in mergeable types; different employers; gap 0–62; A is `probable_salary` | Describes from/to candidate ids, end/start months, gap |
+
+Edge cases:
+
+- Fewer than two candidates → passthrough, no warnings.
+- Candidates with no transaction dates are excluded from the indexed pair scan.
+- Same employer on both streams → pair skipped (no warning).
+- B type not in mergeable set → metadata-only `possible_employment_transition` (no warning).
+- Multiple B candidates for one A → first qualifying merge wins; others may still annotate metadata.
+- Absorbed B candidates are omitted from the output list.
+
+---
+
+## Sequence diagram
+
+REST per-request flow:
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    participant Client
+    participant Route as EmploymentTransitionRoute
+    participant Tool as EmploymentTransitionTools
+    participant Svc as EmploymentTransitionService
+    participant Audit as AuditBuilder
+
+    Client->>Route: POST /api/v1/scoring/employment-transition
+    Route->>Route: build_context / build_audit
+    Route->>Tool: run_link_employment_transitions(scored, config, audit)
+    Tool->>Svc: link_employment_transitions(scored, config)
+    Svc-->>Tool: linked, transition_warnings
+    Tool->>Svc: override_split_subcandidate_types(linked)
+    Svc-->>Tool: final linked list
+    Tool->>Audit: record phase employment_transition
+    Tool-->>Route: EmploymentTransitionToolResult
+    Route-->>Client: success_response(result)
+```
+
