+# Bank transaction feature extraction (Phase 3)
+
+Per-transaction feature extraction on normalised credit rows. Implements **Design §6.3**, **§5.1** (payment channel), and **FR-009** (description signals). Attaches a `TransactionFeatures` record to each `BankTransaction` for hints, candidate generation, and scoring.
+
+Requires a `WorkingDayCalendar` and merged `AppConfig` (salary keywords, negative signals, payment channels).
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Entry point](#entry-point)
+- [Module layout](#module-layout)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Input / output contract](#input--output-contract)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Logging](#logging)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+- [REST endpoint](#rest-endpoint)
+
+## Entry point
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.feature_extraction import (
+    run_extract_bank_transaction_features,
+)
+
+result = run_extract_bank_transaction_features(
+    normalised,
+    config,
+    calendar,
+    region="EnglandAndWales",
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+enhanced = list(result.transactions)
+features_by_id = {t.id: t.features for t in enhanced if t.features}
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Public API | `channels/tools/feature_extraction/BankTransactionFeatureExtractionTools.py` | `run_extract_bank_transaction_features` |
+| Service | `BankTransactionFeatureExtractionService.py` | Orchestrates channel + description + calendar features |
+| Channel | `PaymentChannelDetector.py` | Token/phrase match against `AppConfig.channels()` |
+| Description | `DescriptionFeatureExtractor.py` | Salary hints, negatives, employer tokens |
+| Config | `config/feature_extraction_config.yaml` | Baseline token sets, schema settings |
+| Keywords | `config/salary_keywords.yaml`, `negative_keywords.yaml` | Merged via `AppConfig` |
+| REST | `channels/rest/routes/FeatureExtractionRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapter |
+
+Audit phase name: `features`.
+
+## Module layout
+
+| Module | Responsibility |
+|---|---|
+| `BankTransactionFeatureExtractionService.py` | Batch/single extraction, calendar features |
+| `PaymentChannelDetector.py` | Payment-rail classification + confidence |
+| `DescriptionFeatureExtractor.py` | Hint/negative phrase matching, employer token extraction |
+| `models/DescriptionSignalConfig.py` | Tiered salary/negative keyword mapping from `AppConfig` |
+| `models/FeatureExtractionConfig.py` | Phase YAML loader |
+
+## Business logic
+
+### Payment channel (`PaymentChannelDetector.detect`)
+
+Matches `description_tokens` against `AppConfig.channels()[channel].positive_tokens` (multi-word phrases supported, longest-first ordering).
+
+| Outcome | Channel | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| No match | `unknown_credit` (or first `canonical_channels` entry) | |
+| Best match | Highest-specificity channel | Specificity = token count in matched phrase |
+
+**Confidence formula** (when a channel matches):
+
+```
+specificity = len(matched_phrase_tokens)
+confidence  = min(0.55 + 0.15 × (specificity − 1), 1.0)
+if source_bank configured:
+    confidence = min(confidence + 0.05, 1.0)
+```
+
+No match → `confidence = 0.30`, channel = unknown.
+
+Also returns `matched_tokens` and `alternative_channels` (other channels with any match).
+
+### Description features (`DescriptionFeatureExtractor.extract`)
+
+**Salary hint tokens** — from `DescriptionSignalConfig.positive_by_strength` (merged `AppConfig.salary_hints_keywords()`):
+
+- Multi-word phrases: contiguous subsequence match in token list (longest phrases first).
+- Single tokens: direct lookup by strength key (`strong`, `medium`, `weak` per config).
+
+**Negative tokens** — phrase match against `negative_by_category` from `AppConfig.negative_signals()`.
+
+**Possible employer tokens** — tokens that pass all filters:
+
+| Excluded when token is… |
+|---|
+| Already a salary hint |
+| In channel stop set (baseline + all channel positive tokens) |
+| In `hint_token_baseline` |
+| In `legal_suffix_tokens` |
+| In `generic_stop_tokens` (from normalisation config) |
+| Pure digits |
+| Length &lt; 2 |
+
+### Calendar features (`BankTransactionFeatureExtractionService._extract_resolved`)
+
+Uses `WorkingDayCalendar` and request `region`:
+
+| Feature | Computation |
+|---|---|
+| `day_of_month` | `date.day` |
+| `weekday` | `date.weekday()` (Mon=0) |
+| `is_month_end` | Last calendar day of month |
+| `is_last_working_day` | `calendar.last_working_day_of_month` |
+| `is_first_working_day` | `calendar.first_working_day_of_month` |
+| `is_bank_holiday_adjacent` | ±1 day neighbour is weekday non-working-day |
+
+### Anchor placeholders
+
+`is_anchor`, `anchor_hint_id`, `ambiguous_anchor` are initialised to `False` / `None` / `False`. Phase 4 (`AnchorFlags.attach_anchor_flags`) sets these after payslip hint application.
+
+## Input / output contract
+
+### Input
+
+`Iterable[BankTransaction]` — Phase 2 output with `normalised_description`, `description_tokens`, `skeleton`.
+
+Also requires:
+
+- `AppConfig` — channels, salary keywords, negative signals
+- `WorkingDayCalendar` — UK working-day logic
+- `region: str` — default `EnglandAndWales`
+
+### Output: `FeatureExtractionBatchResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class FeatureExtractionBatchResult:
+    transactions: tuple[BankTransaction, ...]  # each with .features set
+    warnings: tuple[ValidationWarning, ...]
+```
+
+### `TransactionFeatures` fields
+
+```
+transaction_id                  str
+payment_channel                 str
+payment_channel_confidence      float
+payment_channel_matched_tokens  tuple[str, ...]
+salary_hint_tokens              tuple[str, ...]
+negative_tokens                 tuple[str, ...]
+possible_employer_tokens        tuple[str, ...]
+day_of_month, weekday           int
+is_month_end                    bool
+is_last_working_day             bool
+is_first_working_day            bool
+is_bank_holiday_adjacent        bool
+is_anchor                       bool
+anchor_hint_id                  str | None
+ambiguous_anchor                bool
+```
+
+Downstream code typically builds `features_by_id: dict[str, TransactionFeatures]`.
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+Only **payment channel** carries an explicit confidence in this phase:
+
+| Scenario | `payment_channel_confidence` |
+|---|---|
+| No channel token match | `0.30` |
+| Single-token match | `0.55` |
+| Two-token phrase | `0.70` |
+| Three-token phrase | `0.85` |
+| Four+ tokens | capped at `1.0` |
+| `source_bank` in AppConfig | +`0.05` (capped at `1.0`) |
+
+Salary hints and negative tokens are **boolean presence** signals (token lists), not scored here. Their weights are applied in Phase 10 scoring profiles.
+
+Calendar features are deterministic flags — no confidence attached.
+
+## Configuration
+
+### Phase YAML (`config/feature_extraction_config.yaml`)
+
+| Key | Default | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `schema_validation.enabled` | `true` | Row subschema gate |
+| `schema_validation.strict` | `true` | |
+| `hint_strength_keys` / `salary_hint_strength_keys` | strong, medium, weak | Order for hint tier processing |
+| `channel_token_baseline` | BACS, FPS, CHAPS, … | Excluded from employer tokens |
+| `hint_token_baseline` | PAYROLL, SALARY, WAGE, … | Excluded from employer tokens |
+| `legal_suffix_tokens` | LTD, PLC, LLP, … | Excluded from employer tokens |
+| `canonical_channels` | bacs_or_direct_credit, … | Includes `unknown_credit` |
+
+### AppConfig merges (not in phase YAML)
+
+| Source file | Used for |
+|---|---|
+| `config/salary_keywords.yaml` | Positive hint tiers → `DescriptionSignalConfig` |
+| `config/negative_keywords.yaml` | Negative categories |
+| `config/generic_payment_code_mappings.yaml` | Channel definitions |
+| `config/bank_specific_mappings/*.yaml` | Bank-specific channel tokens |
+| `AppConfig.channels()` | `PaymentChannelDetector` positive tokens |
+
+## Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|---|---|
+| INFO | Phase start/done (`phase=features`) |
+| TRACE | Request JSON, per-transaction channel + hint summary |
+| DEBUG | Schema rejections |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.feature_extraction.BankTransactionFeatureExtractionTools`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[BankTransaction list] --> BATCH[extract_bank_transactions]
+    BATCH --> ROW{For each row}
+    ROW --> SCHEMA[Schema check]
+    SCHEMA -- fail --> WARN[warnings, skip]
+    SCHEMA -- ok --> EX[_extract_resolved]
+    EX --> CH[PaymentChannelDetector.detect]
+    EX --> DESC[DescriptionFeatureExtractor.extract]
+    EX --> CAL[Calendar features]
+    CH --> FEAT[TransactionFeatures]
+    DESC --> FEAT
+    CAL --> FEAT
+    FEAT --> BT[BankTransaction with features]
+    BT --> OUT[FeatureExtractionBatchResult]
+```
+
+### Payment channel decision
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    TOKS[description_tokens] --> SCAN[Scan all channel phrases\nlongest first]
+    SCAN --> BEST{Any match?}
+    BEST -- no --> UNK[unknown_credit, conf=0.30]
+    BEST -- yes --> SPEC[Pick highest token-count match]
+    SPEC --> CONF["conf = min(0.55 + 0.15×(n−1), 1.0)"]
+    CONF --> BANK{source_bank set?}
+    BANK -- yes --> PLUS[+0.05 capped]
+    BANK -- no --> OUT[ChannelMatch]
+    PLUS --> OUT
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+| File | Coverage |
+|---|---|
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/feature_extraction/test_payment_channel.py` | Channel match, confidence formula, alternatives |
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/feature_extraction/test_description_features.py` | Hint/negative/employer token extraction |
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/feature_extraction/test_description_signal_config.py` | AppConfig → signal tier mapping |
+| `tests/feature/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/feature_extraction/test_rest.py` | REST smoke |
+
+## Related modules
+
+- **Phase 2** `normalization/` — supplies tokens and skeleton.
+- **Phase 4** `hints/` — `AnchorFlags.py` enriches anchor fields post-hint.
+- **Phase 5–6** candidate generation — consume `features_by_id`.
+- **Phase 10** `scoring/` — applies weights to hint/negative/channel signals.
+- **`pipeline/calendar/`** — holiday data loaded into `WorkingDayCalendar`.
+
+## REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Tool | `run_extract_bank_transaction_features` |
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/features/extract` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/routes/openapi/run_extract_bank_transaction_features.openapi.yaml` |
+
+**Thread safety:** instantiate `BankTransactionFeatureExtractionService` per request with a fresh `WorkingDayCalendar`. Do not share calendar instances across concurrent REST calls.
