+# Graph clustering (Phase 6)
+
+Similarity-graph candidate generation — the **advanced** path alongside Phase 5 skeleton grouping. Implements **Design §10** (edge scoring, connected components, split/merge heuristics). Emits `CandidateSet` records with `metadata.source = "graph_clustering"`.
+
+Also provides **`dedup_candidate_pool`** (Phase 7 tool) to merge skeleton and graph candidates by transaction-id overlap.
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Entry point](#entry-point)
+- [Module layout](#module-layout)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Input / output contract](#input--output-contract)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Logging](#logging)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+- [REST endpoints](#rest-endpoints)
+
+## Entry point
+
+### Graph clustering
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.graph_clustering import (
+    run_graph_clustering,
+)
+
+result = run_graph_clustering(
+    normalised,
+    features_by_id,
+    config,
+    applied_hints=applied_hints,
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+candidates = list(result.candidates)
+```
+
+### Pool deduplication (Phase 7)
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.graph_clustering import (
+    dedup_candidate_pool,
+)
+
+merged = dedup_candidate_pool(
+    skeleton_candidates,
+    graph_candidates,
+    overlap_threshold=0.90,  # optional; default from config
+)
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Public API | `channels/tools/graph_clustering/GraphClusteringTools.py` | `run_graph_clustering`, `run_dedup_candidate_pool` |
+| Service | `GraphClusteringService.py` | Graph build, cluster, emit |
+| Edge functions | same module | Similarity helpers, `compute_edge_score` |
+| Dedup | same module | `dedup_candidate_pool`, `_absorb_all` |
+| Pattern | `PatternInductionService.py` | Character-level prefix/suffix pre-grouping |
+| REST | `channels/rest/routes/GraphClusteringRoute.py`, `DedupRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapters |
+
+Audit phase name: `graph_clustering`.
+
+## Module layout
+
+| Module | Responsibility |
+|---|---|
+| `GraphClusteringService.py` | Pre-grouping, edge build, components, split/merge, emit |
+| `PatternInductionService.py` | `induce_pattern`, `matches_pattern` for description prefixes |
+| `../hints/AnchorResolution.py` | Anchor txn ids for interim confidence |
+| Edge helpers | `description_similarity`, `date_compatibility`, `amount_similarity`, … |
+
+## Business logic
+
+### Pre-grouping (`build_graph`)
+
+Credits are bucketed before all-pairs comparison:
+
+1. **Employer token buckets** — for each `possible_employer_token`, add credit to that token's bucket.
+2. **Skeleton fallback** — credits with no employer tokens → `__skel__::{skeleton}` bucket.
+3. **Pattern induction** (≤ 100 credits only) — when `induce_pattern` finds a stable 8+ char prefix/suffix with ≥ 50% support, add matching credits to `__pattern__::{signature}` bucket.
+
+Two credits are edge candidates when they share **at least one** bucket. Each unordered pair is scored at most once (deduped via `seen_pairs`).
+
+### Edge score (Design §10.2)
+
+For pair `(A, B)` with features:
+
+```
+edge_score = 0.35 × description_sim
+           + 0.25 × date_compatibility
+           + 0.15 × amount_similarity
+           + 0.15 × payment_channel_compatibility
+           + 0.10 × counterparty_similarity
+           − negative_conflict_penalty
+```
+
+Edges with `final ≥ graph_edge_threshold` (default `0.55`) are retained.
+
+#### Component formulas
+
+**Description similarity** (`description_similarity_with_sequence`):
+
+```
+jaccard = |tokens_A ∩ tokens_B| / |tokens_A ∪ tokens_B|
+seq     = LCS_length / max(len_A, len_B)   # token order
+desc    = 0.90 × jaccard + 0.10 × seq
+```
+
+**Date compatibility** (`date_compatibility`):
+
+| Gap (days) | Score |
+|---|---|
+| Same date | `0.0` |
+| 26–32, 12–16, or 5–9 | `1.0` |
+| 24–34, 10–18, or 3–11 | `0.6` |
+| Same calendar month | `0.3` |
+| Other | `0.1` |
+
+**Amount similarity** (`amount_similarity`, default tolerance 10%):
+
+```
+relative = |a − b| / max(|a|, |b|)
+if relative ≤ tolerance_pct: 1.0
+else: max(0, 1.0 − (relative − tolerance_pct))
+```
+
+**Payment channel compatibility**:
+
+| Condition | Score |
+|---|---|
+| Same known channel | `1.0` |
+| Either is `unknown_credit` | `0.5` |
+| Different known channels | `0.2` |
+
+**Counterparty similarity** — currently `0.5` / `0.4` / `1.0` / `0.2` based on reference equality (placeholder for future counterparty field).
+
+**Negative conflict penalty** — `0.20` when exactly one side has negative tokens; else `0.0`.
+
+### Clustering (`cluster` / `_connected_components`)
+
+Union-find connected components over threshold edges. Clusters sorted deterministically by minimum transaction id; members sorted by date.
+
+### Split / merge (Design §10.4) — `_split_distinct_employers`
+
+**Hard split** — when `_group_by_employer_tokens` finds multiple disjoint token-overlap sub-groups within a cluster, each sub-group ≥ 2 survives; singletons become **orphans**.
+
+**Majority outlier extraction** — single token group:
+
+```
+majority_fingerprint = {tok | count(tok) > len(cluster)/2}
+outlier = txn where majority_fingerprint ⊄ txn.tokens
+```
+
+Orphans extracted only when outliers are a strict minority (&lt; majority count). Preserves payroll-provider-change clusters where only shared employer token (e.g. ACME) exceeds threshold.
+
+Orphans attached to candidate `metadata.orphan_credits` for Phase 9 gap matching.
+
+### Candidate emission (`emit_candidates`)
+
+Skip clusters with &lt; 2 members. Build `CandidateSet`:
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `candidate_set_id` | `graph_{idx:03d}` |
+| `candidate_type` | `unknown_recurring_credit` |
+| `metadata.source` | `graph_clustering` |
+| `metadata.edge_threshold` | Configured threshold |
+| `metadata.induced_pattern_signature` | Optional pattern stamp |
+| Per-txn `confidence_details` | Best/weakest edge breakdown |
+
+### Dedup (`dedup_candidate_pool`)
+
+Merge skeleton + graph candidates when transaction-id overlap ≥ threshold (default 90% of **smaller** set):
+
+```
+overlap = |ids_A ∩ ids_B| / min(|ids_A|, |ids_B|)
+```
+
+Processing order: sort by descending transaction count. On overlap, `_absorb_all`:
+
+- Union transactions (dedupe by id)
+- Keep identity from largest/highest-confidence contributor
+- `confidence = max` across merged sources
+- `metadata.merged_sources` lists all contributing paths
+
+## Input / output contract
+
+### Graph clustering input
+
+```
+normalised:      Sequence[BankTransaction]
+features_by_id:  dict[str, TransactionFeatures]
+config:          AppConfig
+applied_hints:   AppliedHints | None
+```
+
+### Graph clustering output
+
+`GraphClusteringToolResult` with `candidates: tuple[CandidateSet, …]`.
+
+Each transaction in a candidate may carry:
+
+- Interim `confidence` and `confidence_band`
+- `confidence_details` with `graph_edge_best` and optionally `graph_edge_weakest` steps
+
+### Dedup input / output
+
+```
+skeleton_candidates: Sequence[CandidateSet]
+graph_candidates:    Sequence[CandidateSet]
+overlap_threshold:   float = 0.90
+→ tuple[CandidateSet, ...]
+```
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+### Interim candidate confidence (pre-Phase 10)
+
+```
+size_score         = min(1.0, len(members) / 12.0)
+interim_confidence = min(1.0, 0.50 + 0.25 × size_score + (0.15 if anchor_in_cluster else 0.0))
+```
+
+Rounded to 4 dp. Same formula applied per `CandidateTransaction` within the cluster.
+
+### Per-transaction edge audit (`ConfidenceDetail`)
+
+**Best edge** — always emitted when cluster has internal edges:
+
+```
+step = "graph_edge_best"
+confidence_step = edge.final
+reasoning = "0.35×desc + 0.25×date + … − penalty = final"
+```
+
+**Weakest edge** — when multiple peers and weakest &lt; best:
+
+```
+step = "graph_edge_weakest"
+flag "⚠ borderline absorption" when final < threshold + 0.05
+```
+
+### Edge score as similarity confidence
+
+The edge `final` score ∈ [0, 1] acts as the pairwise link confidence. Only edges ≥ `graph_edge_threshold` participate in clustering.
+
+### Confidence bands
+
+Same cuts as skeleton grouping:
+
+| Score | Band |
+|---|---|
+| ≥ 0.85 | `high` |
+| ≥ 0.70 | `medium_high` |
+| ≥ 0.55 | `medium` |
+| ≥ 0.40 | `low` |
+| &lt; 0.40 | `very_low` |
+
+Phase 10 scoring replaces interim values.
+
+## Configuration
+
+From `AppConfig.candidate_generation()` (`pipeline/scoring/config/candidate_generation.yaml`):
+
+| Key | Default | Used by |
+|---|---|---|
+| `graph_edge_threshold` | `0.55` | Edge retention cutoff |
+| `dedup_txn_id_overlap_pct` | `0.90` | `dedup_candidate_pool` default threshold |
+
+### Module constants
+
+| Constant | Value | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| Edge weights | 0.35 / 0.25 / 0.15 / 0.15 / 0.10 | Description / date / amount / channel / counterparty |
+| Negative penalty | `0.20` | Single-sided negative token |
+| Amount tolerance | `0.10` | `amount_similarity` default |
+| Pattern induction cap | 100 credits | Runtime guard for O(n²) buckets |
+| `min_support` (pre-group) | 0.5 | Pattern induction in `build_graph` |
+| `min_support` (emit stamp) | 0.6 | Pattern on emitted candidate |
+
+## Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|---|---|
+| INFO | Phase start/done: credit count, edge count, cluster count |
+| DEBUG | Pre-group bucket sizes, split/orphan decisions |
+| TRACE | Per-edge breakdown for borderline pairs |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.graph_clustering.GraphClusteringTools`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[credits + features_by_id] --> PRE[Pre-group buckets\nemployer / skeleton / pattern]
+    PRE --> PAIRS[All pairs within shared buckets]
+    PAIRS --> EDGE[compute_edge_score]
+    EDGE --> TH{final ≥ threshold?}
+    TH -- no --> DROP[Discard edge]
+    TH -- yes --> KEEP[Add to edge map]
+    KEEP --> CC[Connected components]
+    CC --> SPLIT[_split_distinct_employers]
+    SPLIT --> EMIT[emit_candidates ≥ 2 members]
+    EMIT --> OUT[GraphClusteringToolResult]
+```
+
+### Edge score breakdown
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    DESC["desc 35%"] --> SUM[edge final]
+    DATE["date 25%"] --> SUM
+    AMT["amount 15%"] --> SUM
+    CH["channel 15%"] --> SUM
+    CP["counterparty 10%"] --> SUM
+    NEG["− penalty"] --> SUM
+```
+
+### Dedup merge
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    SK[skeleton candidates] --> POOL[Sort by txn count desc]
+    GR[graph candidates] --> POOL
+    POOL --> CAND{For each candidate}
+    CAND --> OV{Overlap ≥ threshold\nwith survivor?}
+    OV -- no --> ADD[Append to survivors]
+    OV -- yes --> ABS[_absorb_all union txns\nmax confidence]
+    ABS --> ADD
+    ADD --> OUT[Deduplicated pool]
+```
+
