+# Bank transaction normalisation (Phase 2)
+
+Deterministic text normalisation for validated credit rows. Implements **Design §6.1**, **§8.1**, and **§10.5** (skeleton key generation). Produces canonical `BankTransaction` records with `normalised_description`, `description_tokens`, and `skeleton` — the skeleton field is consumed directly by Phase 5 skeleton grouping.
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Entry point](#entry-point)
+- [Module layout](#module-layout)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Input / output contract](#input--output-contract)
+- [Confidence and scoring](#confidence-and-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Logging](#logging)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+- [REST endpoint](#rest-endpoint)
+
+## Entry point
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.normalization import (
+    run_normalize_bank_transactions,
+)
+
+result = run_normalize_bank_transactions(
+    rows,  # Iterable[RawBankTransaction | Mapping]
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+normalised = list(result.transactions)
+# result.warnings → schema validation warnings for rejected rows
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Public API | `channels/tools/normalization/BankTransactionNormalizationTools.py` | `run_normalize_bank_transactions`, `normalize_bank_transaction` |
+| Service | `BankTransactionNormalizationService.py` | `normalise_text`, `tokenise`, `skeleton_of`, batch normalisation |
+| Config | `config/normalization_config.yaml` | Stop tokens, legal suffix map, regex patterns |
+| Models | `models/NormalizationConfig.py`, `NormalizationResult.py`, … | Config loader + result DTOs |
+| Schema | `schemas/normalization.schema.json` | Optional row subschema validation |
+| REST | `channels/rest/routes/NormalizationRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapter |
+
+Audit phase name: `normalise`.
+
+## Module layout
+
+| Module | Responsibility |
+|---|---|
+| `BankTransactionNormalizationService.py` | Core normalisation pipeline |
+| `models/NormalizationConfig.py` | YAML loader for phase config |
+| `models/NormalizationTextPatterns.py` | Compiled regex bundle |
+| `schemas/normalization.schema.json` | `bank_transaction` subschema for `SchemaCheckService` |
+
+## Business logic
+
+### Text normalisation (`normalise_text`)
+
+Applied to the raw description string:
+
+1. **Unicode** — NFKD decompose; strip combining marks (accent removal).
+2. **Case** — upper-case ASCII.
+3. **Legal suffixes** — word-boundary replace per `legal_suffix_map` (longest phrases first in YAML order).
+4. **Punctuation** — replace non `[A-Z0-9 ]` with space (`text_patterns.punct`).
+5. **Whitespace** — collapse runs (`text_patterns.whitespace`); strip.
+
+Empty input → `""`.
+
+### Tokenisation (`tokenise`)
+
+Split normalised text on spaces; drop empty tokens. Returns `tuple[str, ...]`.
+
+### Skeleton key (`skeleton_of`)
+
+Recall-oriented grouping key for Phase 5. Built from the **raw** description (re-normalises internally):
+
+| Step | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| Empty / None | Return `empty_skeleton_placeholder` (`__EMPTY__`) |
+| Long digit tokens | Drop tokens matching `long_digit_token` (`^\d{4,}$`) |
+| Stop tokens | Drop tokens in `generic_stop_tokens` |
+| Trailing digits | Strip suffix digits from token (`trailing_digits`: `(?<=[A-Z])\d{2,}$`) |
+| Post-trim stop | Drop if trimmed token is empty or a stop token |
+| Result | Space-join surviving tokens, or placeholder if none remain |
+
+Skeleton intentionally keeps employer-like tokens while removing payment-rail noise and long reference numbers.
+
+### Batch processing (`normalize_bank_transactions`)
+
+For each input row:
+
+1. Resolve payload dict + transaction id.
+2. Run `SchemaCheckService` against `bank_transaction` subschema (when enabled).
+3. Invalid rows → warnings, skipped.
+4. Valid rows → `_normalize_resolved` → `BankTransaction`.
+
+### Output `BankTransaction`
+
+Wraps the original `RawBankTransaction` (`raw`) plus:
+
+```
+normalised_description   str
+description_tokens       tuple[str, ...]
+skeleton                 str
+```
+
+`amount`, `date`, and `id` are derived properties on `BankTransaction` from `raw`.
+
+## Input / output contract
+
+### Input
+
+`Iterable[RawBankTransaction | Mapping[str, Any]]` — typically Phase 1 output.
+
+Required mapping keys when not using dataclass: `id`, `date`, `description`, `debit_amount`, `credit_amount`.
+
+### Output: `NormalizationBatchResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class NormalizationBatchResult:
+    transactions: tuple[BankTransaction, ...]
+    warnings: tuple[ValidationWarning, ...]
+```
+
+Single-row API returns `NormalizationResult(transaction=…, warnings=…)`.
+
+Tool wrapper: `NormalizationToolResult`.
+
+## Confidence and scoring
+
+Normalisation does **not** produce confidence scores. The **skeleton string** is the primary downstream signal:
+
+- Identical skeleton → same bucket in Phase 5.
+- Skeleton quality affects plausibility indirectly via group cohesion; no numeric score is assigned here.
+
+Schema validation failures emit `ValidationWarning` entries (code from `SchemaCheckService`) but do not affect other rows in the batch.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Source: `config/normalization_config.yaml` via `load_normalization_config()`.
+
+| Key | Default (YAML) | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `generic_stop_tokens` | REF, PAYMENT, TRANSFER, … | Dropped from skeleton |
+| `legal_suffix_map` | PUBLIC LIMITED COMPANY→PLC, LIMITED→LTD | Applied before tokenisation |
+| `empty_skeleton_placeholder` | `__EMPTY__` | Empty/meaningless descriptions |
+| `default_currency` | GBP | Metadata default |
+| `default_direction` | credit | Metadata default |
+| `schema_validation.enabled` | `true` | Toggle subschema checks |
+| `schema_validation.strict` | `true` | Strict schema mode |
+| `text_patterns.punct` | `[^A-Z0-9 ]+` | Punctuation strip regex |
+| `text_patterns.whitespace` | `\s+` | Whitespace collapse |
+| `text_patterns.long_digit_token` | `^\d{4,}$` | Reference numbers removed from skeleton |
+| `text_patterns.trailing_digits` | `(?<=[A-Z])\d{2,}$` | Trailing numeric suffix trim |
+
+## Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|---|---|
+| INFO | Phase start/done (`phase=normalise`) |
+| TRACE | Request JSON via `@tool` wrapper |
+| DEBUG | Per-row schema rejection details |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.normalization.BankTransactionNormalizationTools`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[RawBankTransaction rows] --> BATCH[normalize_bank_transactions]
+    BATCH --> ROW{For each row}
+    ROW --> SCHEMA[SchemaCheckService.check\nbank_transaction subschema]
+    SCHEMA -- invalid --> WARN[Append warnings, skip row]
+    SCHEMA -- valid --> RESOLVE[_normalize_resolved]
+    RESOLVE --> TEXT[normalise_text]
+    TEXT --> TOK[tokenise]
+    RESOLVE --> SKEL[skeleton_of raw description]
+    TEXT --> BT[BankTransaction]
+    TOK --> BT
+    SKEL --> BT
+    BT --> OUT[NormalizationBatchResult]
+    WARN --> ROW
+```
+
+### Skeleton derivation (detail)
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    RAW[raw.description] --> NORM[normalise_text]
+    NORM --> TOKS[Split tokens]
+    TOKS --> FILT{Filter}
+    FILT -->|drop| LONG[long digit tokens]
+    FILT -->|drop| STOP[generic_stop_tokens]
+    FILT -->|trim| TRAIL[trailing digits]
+    FILT --> KEEP[Surviving tokens]
+    KEEP --> JOIN[Space join]
+    JOIN --> SK[skeleton key]
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+| File | Coverage |
+|---|---|
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/normalization/test_normalisation.py` | `normalise_text`, `skeleton_of`, legal suffix, stop tokens |
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/normalization/test_bank_transaction_normalization_tools.py` | Tool wrapper, batch API |
+| `tests/feature/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/normalization/test_rest.py` | REST endpoint smoke |
+
+## Related modules
+
+- **Phase 1** `validation/` — supplies `RawBankTransaction` input.
+- **Phase 3** `feature_extraction/` — reads `description_tokens`, `skeleton`.
+- **Phase 5** `skeleton_grouping/` — buckets by `skeleton`.
+- **`EmployerHintMatcher.py`** (hints) — reuses `default_service().normalise_text` for employer tokenisation.
+
+## REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Tool | `run_normalize_bank_transactions` |
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/normalization/normalize` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/routes/openapi/run_normalize_bank_transactions.openapi.yaml` |
+
+Services load immutable config at construction. `default_service()` is a process-wide singleton — safe because `NormalizationConfig` is frozen and the service has no per-request mutable state beyond local variables.
