+# Candidate Ranking and Near-Miss Capping
+
+**Pipeline phase:** 12 — `ranking`
+
+Sorts scored candidates by confidence, applies a return threshold and hard caps, and splits the
+pool into **returned** candidates (primary output) and **near-miss** candidates (secondary output
+with reason tags).
+
+This is the last deterministic transformation in the salary pipeline before the optional audit
+snapshot. The salary-extractor maps output to `BankTransactionResult.candidate_sets` and
+`rejected_or_near_miss_sets`.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Purpose and pipeline position](#purpose-and-pipeline-position)
+- [Entry points](#entry-points)
+- [Inputs and outputs](#inputs-and-outputs)
+- [Design](#design)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Warnings and edge cases](#warnings-and-edge-cases)
+- [Sequence diagram](#sequence-diagram)
+- [Key source files](#key-source-files)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+
+---
+
+## Purpose and pipeline position
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    ET[11 employment_transition\nrun_link_employment_transitions] --> NK[negative_keyword partition\nsalary-extractor only]
+    NK --> R[12 ranking\nrun_rank_candidates]
+    R --> OUT[returned + near_miss candidates]
+    R --> AUDIT[AuditBuilder snapshot\noptional]
+```
+
+| Direction | Phase | Tool |
+|-----------|-------|------|
+| Upstream | 11 — employment transition | `run_link_employment_transitions` |
+| This phase | 12 — ranking | `run_rank_candidates` |
+| Downstream | Orchestrator result | `candidate_sets` / `rejected_or_near_miss_sets` |
+
+Ranking does not alter confidence values — it filters, sorts, caps, and tags near-misses.
+
+---
+
+## Entry points
+
+### Tool (primary)
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.ranking import run_rank_candidates
+
+result = run_rank_candidates(
+    scored,
+    config,
+    max_candidates=10,          # optional override
+    max_near_misses=10,         # optional override
+    return_threshold=0.40,      # optional override
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+returned = list(result.returned)
+near_misses = list(result.near_misses)
+```
+
+Lazy import path (same function):
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.ranking.RankingTools import run_rank_candidates
+```
+
+### Service (direct logic)
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.ranking.RankingService import (
+    RankingConfig,
+    rank_candidates,
+    resolve_ranking_config,
+    tag_near_miss,
+)
+
+ranking = resolve_ranking_config(config, return_threshold=0.40)
+returned, near_misses, ranking = rank_candidates(scored, ranking)
+```
+
+### REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|----------|-------|
+| Tool | `run_rank_candidates` |
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/ranking/rank` |
+| Route | `channels/rest/routes/RankingRoute.py` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/routes/openapi/run_rank_candidates.openapi.yaml` |
+
+Audit phase name: `ranking`.
+
+### Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|-------|---------|
+| INFO | Phase start: `scored=N`; phase done summary via tool wrapper |
+| DEBUG | Phase done: threshold, returned count, near_miss counts by reason |
+| TRACE | Per returned / near-miss candidate: id, type, confidence, reason |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.ranking.RankingTools`.
+
+Services are stateless and instantiated per call. REST handlers build a fresh `RouteContext` per
+request — do not share mutable state across threads.
+
+---
+
+## Inputs and outputs
+
+### Input
+
+`Sequence[CandidateSet]` — typically post phase-11 employment linking (after optional
+negative-keyword partition in the orchestrator).
+
+| Field | Usage |
+|-------|-------|
+| `confidence` | Sort key and threshold split |
+| `candidate_set_id` | Tie-break (ascending when confidence equal) |
+| `candidate_type`, `confidence_band` | TRACE logging only |
+| `metadata` | Copied and extended with `near_miss_reason` for near-misses |
+
+Also accepts optional kwargs forwarded to `resolve_ranking_config` and `AppConfig`.
+
+### Output: `RankingToolResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class RankingToolResult(BaseToolModel):
+    returned: tuple[CandidateSet, ...] = ()
+    near_misses: tuple[CandidateSet, ...] = ()
+    return_threshold: float = 0.40
+    max_candidates: int = 10
+    max_near_misses: int = 10
+```
+
+Orchestrator mapping:
+
+```python
+SalaryDetectionResult(
+    candidate_sets=tuple(returned),
+    rejected_or_near_miss_sets=tuple(near_misses),
+    metadata={
+        "return_threshold": …,
+        "max_candidates": …,
+        "max_near_misses": …,
+        …
+    },
+)
+```
+
+This module does **not** emit `ValidationWarning` entries under normal operation.
+
+---
+
+## Design
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[scored from phase 11] --> RESOLVE[resolve_ranking_config\nYAML + kwargs]
+    RESOLVE --> SORT[Sort by -confidence, candidate_set_id]
+    SORT --> SPLIT{confidence ≥ return_threshold?}
+    SPLIT --> ABOVE[above list]
+    SPLIT --> BELOW[below list]
+    ABOVE --> RET[returned = above[:max_candidates]]
+    ABOVE --> OVER[cap_overflow = above[max_candidates:]]
+    OVER --> NM1[tag near_miss_reason=cap_overflow]
+    BELOW --> NM2[tag below_threshold\nup to remaining slots]
+    NM1 --> MERGE[Combine + truncate to max_near_misses]
+    NM2 --> MERGE
+    RET --> OUT[RankingToolResult]
+    MERGE --> OUT
+```
+
+---
+
+## Business logic
+
+1. **Resolve config** — merge YAML defaults with optional kwargs (`return_threshold`,
+   `max_candidates`, `max_near_misses`).
+2. **Stable sort** — `(-confidence, candidate_set_id)` so ties break deterministically on the
+   id assigned at candidate generation.
+3. **Threshold split** — candidates with `confidence >= return_threshold` go to the above pool;
+   others go to the below pool.
+4. **Return cap** — `returned = above[:max_candidates]`.
+5. **Cap overflow** — `cap_overflow = above[max_candidates:]`; each tagged
+   `metadata.near_miss_reason = "cap_overflow"`.
+6. **Below-threshold near-misses** — remaining slots filled from below pool, tagged
+   `"below_threshold"`.
+7. **Near-miss cap** — combined near-miss list truncated to `max_near_misses`.
+
+Core algorithm:
+
+```python
+ordered = sorted(scored, key=lambda c: (-c.confidence, c.candidate_set_id))
+
+above = [c for c in ordered if c.confidence >= return_threshold]
+below = [c for c in ordered if c.confidence < return_threshold]
+
+returned = above[:max_candidates]
+cap_overflow = above[max_candidates:]
+
+remaining_near_miss_slots = max(0, max_near_misses - len(cap_overflow))
+below_kept = below[:remaining_near_miss_slots]
+
+near_misses = [tag_near_miss(c, "cap_overflow") for c in cap_overflow]
+near_misses += [tag_near_miss(c, "below_threshold") for c in below_kept]
+near_misses = near_misses[:max_near_misses]
+```
+
+### Near-miss slot accounting
+
+`cap_overflow` candidates **consume** near-miss slots first. Example with
+`max_near_misses=10`:
+
+- 15 above-threshold, `max_candidates=10` → 5 cap_overflow near-misses, 5 slots left for
+  below-threshold candidates.
+- If cap_overflow alone exceeds `max_near_misses`, the list is truncated to `max_near_misses`
+  (below-threshold candidates may be dropped entirely).
+
+Near-miss tagging uses immutable `dataclasses.replace` to set `metadata.near_miss_reason`
+without mutating the input candidate.
+
+### Near-miss reason values
+
+| Reason | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| `cap_overflow` | Passed threshold but trimmed by `max_candidates` |
+| `below_threshold` | Below threshold; kept up to remaining near-miss slots |
+
+---
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+Ranking uses **existing** candidate confidence from phase 10 scoring (and any merge adjustments
+from phase 11). No rescoring, caps, or `ConfidenceDetail` steps are added.
+
+| Operation | Confidence impact |
+|-----------|-------------------|
+| Sort | Reads `confidence` only |
+| Threshold split | Compares against `return_threshold` (default 0.40) |
+| Return / near-miss split | No modification to `confidence` or `confidence_band` |
+| Near-miss tag | Metadata only (`near_miss_reason`) |
+
+Effective threshold and caps are echoed on `RankingToolResult` and typically copied into
+orchestrator result metadata.
+
+---
+
+## Configuration
+
+Resolved by `resolve_ranking_config(config, **overrides)`:
+
+| Effective field | Config path | Default | Override |
+|-----------------|-------------|---------|----------|
+| `return_threshold` | `thresholds.return_threshold` | `0.40` | `run_rank_candidates` kwarg |
+| `max_candidates` | `candidate_generation.max_candidates_to_return` | `10` | kwarg |
+| `max_near_misses` | `candidate_generation.max_near_misses` | `10` | kwarg |
+
+Source YAML files (merged by `ConfigLoader` / `AppConfig`):
+
+- `pipeline/scoring/config/scoring_config.yaml` → `thresholds.return_threshold`
+- `pipeline/scoring/config/candidate_generation.yaml` → `max_candidates_to_return`, `max_near_misses`
+
+Priority (highest wins):
+
+```
+detect_salary_candidates kwarg  →  payload options  →  merged YAML default
+```
+
+No dedicated YAML under `pipeline/ranking/config/` — ranking reuses scoring-phase config keys.
+
+---
+
+## Warnings and edge cases
+
+| Situation | Behaviour |
+|-----------|-----------|
+| Empty input | Returns empty `returned` and `near_misses` with resolved config defaults |
+| All below threshold | `returned` empty; up to `max_near_misses` tagged `below_threshold` |
+| All above threshold, under cap | All in `returned`; empty near-misses |
+| Tie on confidence | Lower `candidate_set_id` wins (lexicographic) |
+| `max_near_misses=0` | No near-misses even when cap overflow exists |
+
+No `ValidationWarning` codes are emitted by this phase.
+
+---
+
+## Sequence diagram
+
+REST per-request flow:
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    participant Client
+    participant Route as RankingRoute
+    participant Tool as RankingTools
+    participant Svc as RankingService
+    participant Audit as AuditBuilder
+
+    Client->>Route: POST /api/v1/ranking/rank
+    Route->>Route: build_context / build_audit
+    Route->>Tool: run_rank_candidates(scored, config, overrides…)
+    Tool->>Svc: resolve_ranking_config(config, …)
+    Svc-->>Tool: RankingConfig
+    Tool->>Svc: rank_candidates(scored, ranking)
+    Svc-->>Tool: returned, near_misses, ranking
+    Tool->>Audit: record phase ranking
+    Tool-->>Route: RankingToolResult
+    Route-->>Client: success_response(result)
+```
+
+Orchestrator post-step (salary-extractor): `audit.record_candidates(returned + near_misses)`.
