+# Skeleton grouping (Phase 5)
+
+Recall-oriented candidate generation by **normalised-description skeleton**. Implements **FR-018** and **Design §10.5** (skeleton path). Runs **before** Phase 6 graph clustering and emits `CandidateSet` records with `metadata.source = "skeleton_grouping"`.
+
+The skeleton path optimises for **recall** (find plausible recurring credit streams). Classification is deferred — emitted candidates use `candidate_type = "unknown_recurring_credit"` until Phase 10 scoring.
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Entry point](#entry-point)
+- [Module layout](#module-layout)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Input / output contract](#input--output-contract)
+- [Confidence scoring](#confidence-scoring)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Logging](#logging)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+- [REST endpoint](#rest-endpoint)
+
+## Entry point
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.skeleton_grouping import (
+    run_emit_skeleton_candidates,
+)
+
+result = run_emit_skeleton_candidates(
+    normalised,
+    features_by_id,
+    config,
+    applied_hints=applied_hints,  # optional
+    threshold=None,               # optional override
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+candidates = list(result.candidates)
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Public API | `channels/tools/skeleton_grouping/SkeletonGroupingTools.py` | `run_emit_skeleton_candidates` |
+| Service | `SkeletonGroupingService.py` | Grouping, plausibility, emission |
+| Models | `models/SkeletonGroupingToolResult.py` | `candidates` tuple |
+| Shared stats | `../scoring/AmountFeatureService.py` | `cluster_stats`, CV computation |
+| REST | `channels/rest/routes/SkeletonGroupingRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapter |
+
+Audit phase name: `skeleton_grouping`.
+
+## Module layout
+
+| Module | Responsibility |
+|---|---|
+| `SkeletonGroupingService.py` | End-to-end skeleton path |
+| `../hints/AnchorResolution.py` | `group_has_anchor`, feature-flag mode |
+| `../hints/applicators/SalaryApplicator.py` | `band_modifier` for amount plausibility |
+| `../scoring/AmountFeatureService.py` | `cluster_stats` → coefficient of variation |
+
+## Business logic
+
+### Step 1 — Group by skeleton (`group_by_skeleton`)
+
+Bucket credits by `BankTransaction.skeleton` (computed in Phase 2 `skeleton_of`). Deterministic iteration order: sorted skeleton string keys.
+
+### Step 2 — Filter by minimum size
+
+Skip groups with fewer than `min_skeleton_group_size` members (default `2`).
+
+### Step 3 — Plausibility scoring (`score_group_plausibility`)
+
+Four-axis score with fixed weights:
+
+```
+base = 0.40 × date_plausibility
+     + 0.30 × amount_plausibility
+     + 0.15 × anchor_presence
+     + 0.15 × (1 − negative_signal_share)
+
+if anchor_presence ≥ 1.0:
+    final = max(base, 0.55)   # anchor floor
+else:
+    final = base
+```
+
+All axis values rounded to 4 dp in `PlausibilityScore`.
+
+#### Date plausibility (`_date_plausibility`)
+
+Two sub-signals combined 50/50:
+
+**Coverage** — distinct `(year, month)` count divided by calendar span months between first and last credit (inclusive), capped at `1.0`.
+
+**Gap regularity** — among adjacent sorted credits (same-day pairs skipped):
+
+- Count gaps where `26 ≤ gap_days ≤ 32` as "good monthly"
+- `gap_regularity = good_gaps / total_gaps` (0 if no gaps)
+
+#### Amount plausibility (`_amount_plausibility`)
+
+Uses `cluster_stats(amounts).coefficient_of_variation` (CV):
+
+| CV range | cv_score |
+|---|---|
+| ≤ 0.02 | `1.0` |
+| ≥ 0.20 | `0.0` |
+| between | `1.0 − (cv − 0.02) / 0.18` (linear decay) |
+
+When salary band present (`AppliedHints.effective_monthly`):
+
+```
+amount_plausibility = cv_score × band_modifier(median_amount, band)
+```
+
+`band_modifier` — see Phase 4 hints README (FR-017).
+
+#### Anchor presence (`_anchor_presence`)
+
+`1.0` if any group member is an anchor transaction (via `AnchorResolution.group_has_anchor`); else `0.0`.
+
+#### Negative signal share (`_negative_signal_share`)
+
+Fraction of group members with non-empty `features.negative_tokens`.
+
+### Step 4 — Threshold filter and emit (`emit_plausible_sets`)
+
+Emit groups where `final ≥ skeleton_plausibility_threshold` (default `0.45`).
+
+Each emitted `CandidateSet`:
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `candidate_set_id` | `skeleton_{idx:03d}` (stable sort order) |
+| `candidate_type` | `unknown_recurring_credit` |
+| `confidence` | `PlausibilityScore.final` |
+| `confidence_band` | Derived from final (see below) |
+| `detected_pattern.frequency` | `monthly_candidate` |
+| `detected_pattern.payday_model` | `unknown_pending_phase6` |
+| `detected_pattern.possible_employer_tokens` | Intersection across members |
+| `detected_pattern.payment_channel` | Mode (dominant count) |
+| `metadata.source` | `skeleton_grouping` |
+| `metadata.skeleton_key` | Skeleton string |
+| `metadata.plausibility` | Per-axis breakdown dict |
+
+## Input / output contract
+
+### Input
+
+```
+normalised:      Iterable[BankTransaction]
+features_by_id:  dict[str, TransactionFeatures]
+config:          AppConfig
+applied_hints:   AppliedHints | None   # salary band + anchors
+threshold:       float | None          # overrides YAML default
+```
+
+### Output: `SkeletonGroupingToolResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class SkeletonGroupingToolResult:
+    candidates: tuple[CandidateSet, ...]
+```
+
+Each `CandidateSet.transactions` holds `CandidateTransaction` rows sorted by date.
+
+## Confidence scoring
+
+Skeleton plausibility **is** the interim confidence for this path.
+
+### Axis weights
+
+| Axis | Weight | Range |
+|---|---|---|
+| Date plausibility | 40% | [0, 1] |
+| Amount plausibility | 30% | [0, 1] |
+| Anchor presence | 15% | {0, 1} |
+| 1 − negative share | 15% | [0, 1] |
+
+### Anchor floor
+
+When a payslip anchor lands in the group:
+
+```
+final = max(base, 0.55)
+```
+
+Prevents a confirmed anchor group from scoring below medium despite noisy amount/date signals.
+
+### Confidence bands (`_band_for_score`)
+
+Aligned with Phase 10 cuts for uniform detector output:
+
+| Final score | Band |
+|---|---|
+| ≥ 0.85 | `high` |
+| ≥ 0.70 | `medium_high` |
+| ≥ 0.55 | `medium` |
+| ≥ 0.40 | `low` |
+| &lt; 0.40 | `very_low` |
+
+Phase 10 scoring **replaces** `confidence`, `candidate_type`, and `score_breakdown` — skeleton values are interim.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Merged via `AppConfig.candidate_generation()` from `pipeline/scoring/config/candidate_generation.yaml`:
+
+| Key | Default | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `min_skeleton_group_size` | `2` | Minimum credits per skeleton group |
+| `skeleton_plausibility_threshold` | `0.45` | Emit cutoff; overridable per call |
+
+### Module constants (not YAML)
+
+| Constant | Value | Location |
+|---|---|---|
+| `_GOOD_MONTHLY_GAP_DAYS` | `(26, 32)` | `SkeletonGroupingService.py` |
+| Plausibility weights | 0.40 / 0.30 / 0.15 / 0.15 | same |
+| Anchor floor | `0.55` | same |
+
+### Hint-derived (Phase 4)
+
+| Input | Effect on scoring |
+|---|---|
+| `AppliedHints` salary band | Amount plausibility via `band_modifier` |
+| Payslip anchors | Anchor presence axis + floor |
+
+## Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|---|---|
+| INFO | Phase start/done: group count, emitted candidate count |
+| DEBUG | Per skeleton group: axis scores, emit/skip reason |
+| TRACE | Skeleton key, member ids, threshold comparison |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.skeleton_grouping.SkeletonGroupingTools`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[normalised + features_by_id] --> GRP[group_by_skeleton]
+    GRP --> LOOP{For each skeleton group}
+    LOOP --> SIZE{len ≥ min_group_size?}
+    SIZE -- no --> SKIP1[Skip group]
+    SIZE -- yes --> SCORE[score_group_plausibility]
+    SCORE --> DATE[date: coverage + gap regularity]
+    SCORE --> AMT[amount: CV score × band_modifier]
+    SCORE --> ANC[anchor_presence 0 or 1]
+    SCORE --> NEG[negative_signal_share]
+    DATE --> COMB[Weighted sum + anchor floor]
+    AMT --> COMB
+    ANC --> COMB
+    NEG --> COMB
+    COMB --> TH{final ≥ threshold?}
+    TH -- no --> SKIP2[Skip group]
+    TH -- yes --> EMIT[CandidateSet skeleton_NNN]
+    EMIT --> OUT[SkeletonGroupingToolResult]
+```
+
+### Plausibility formula
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    D[date 40%] --> SUM[Weighted base]
+    A[amount 30%] --> SUM
+    AP[anchor 15%] --> SUM
+    NS["1−neg 15%"] --> SUM
+    SUM --> FLOOR{anchor = 1?}
+    FLOOR -- yes --> MAX["max(base, 0.55)"]
+    FLOOR -- no --> FINAL[final = base]
+    MAX --> FINAL
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+| File | Coverage |
+|---|---|
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/skeleton_grouping/test_skeleton.py` | Grouping, emission, candidate shape |
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/skeleton_grouping/test_skeleton_plausibility.py` | Date/amount/anchor/negative axis math, anchor floor |
+
+## Related modules
+
+- **Phase 2** `normalization/` — produces `skeleton` keys.
+- **Phase 4** `hints/` — salary band and anchor inputs.
+- **Phase 6** `graph_clustering/` — parallel advanced path; merged in Phase 7 dedup.
+- **Phase 7** `dedup_candidate_pool` — merges skeleton + graph candidates by txn-id overlap.
+- **Phase 10** `scoring/` — canonical classifier replacing interim type/confidence.
+
+## REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Tool | `run_emit_skeleton_candidates` |
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/skeleton/emit` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/routes/openapi/run_emit_skeleton_candidates.openapi.yaml` |
+
+`SkeletonGroupingService` is constructed per call with immutable `AppConfig` — safe for concurrent REST requests when each request has its own config snapshot.
