+# Bank transaction validation (Phase 1)
+
+Schema-checks and normalises caller rows before any downstream pipeline work. Implements **FR-001** (payload contract) and **FR-002** (credit-only input). Emits validated `RawBankTransaction` records, `ValidationWarning` entries, and an optional **early exit** when no transactions are present.
+
+Runs first in the full salary-detection pipeline. Downstream phases assume ISO-normalised dates, non-negative amounts, and credit-only rows.
+
+## Table of contents
+
+- [Entry point](#entry-point)
+- [Module layout](#module-layout)
+- [Business logic](#business-logic)
+- [Input / output contract](#input--output-contract)
+- [Confidence and warnings](#confidence-and-warnings)
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Logging](#logging)
+- [Flow](#flow)
+- [Tests](#tests)
+- [Related modules](#related-modules)
+- [REST endpoint](#rest-endpoint)
+
+## Entry point
+
+```python
+from nw_agcore_bank_transactions.pipeline.validation import (
+    run_validate_bank_transaction_payload,
+)
+
+result = run_validate_bank_transaction_payload(
+    payload,
+    mode="lenient",  # or "strict"
+    audit=audit,
+    warnings=warnings,
+)
+transactions = list(result.transactions)
+# result.warnings → ValidationWarning tuples
+# result.early_exit → True when transactions key missing/null
+```
+
+| Layer | File | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Public API | `channels/tools/validation/BankTransactionValidationTools.py` | `BankTransactionValidationTools`, `run_validate_bank_transaction_payload` |
+| Service | `BankTransactionValidationService.py` | `validate_payload`, row normalisation |
+| Helpers | same module | `validate_and_normalise_rows`, `validate_payload_fields`, `validate_schema` |
+| Schema | `schemas/input.schema.json` | JSON Schema for raw dict fixtures (test-only runtime validation) |
+| Models | `../_models/requests/BankTransactionRequest.py` | Typed request DTO |
+| REST | `channels/rest/routes/ValidationRoute.py` | Stateless FastAPI adapter |
+
+Audit phase name: `validate`.
+
+## Module layout
+
+| Module | Responsibility |
+|---|---|
+| `BankTransactionValidationService.py` | Orchestrates payload + row validation |
+| `schemas/input.schema.json` | Structural contract for API/fixture dicts |
+| `routes/ValidationRoute.py` | Phase-local route stub (canonical REST lives under `channels/rest/`) |
+
+## Business logic
+
+### Payload-level checks (`validate_payload_fields`)
+
+Semantic checks on a typed `BankTransactionRequest` (jsonschema validation of raw dicts is **test-only** via `validate_schema`):
+
+| Field | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| `analysis_id` | Non-empty string |
+| `country_region` | One of `EnglandAndWales`, `Scotland`, `NorthernIreland`, `UnknownDefaultEnglandAndWales`, or omitted |
+| `validation_mode` | `lenient` or `strict` |
+
+### Row-level checks (`_validate_single`)
+
+For each transaction row:
+
+1. **Id** — required non-empty string.
+2. **Amounts** — parse to `Decimal`; both must be ≥ 0; cannot both be positive; cannot both be zero unless the row is a balance marker.
+3. **Balance markers** — when `is_brought_forward` or `is_final_balance` is true, both amounts must be zero.
+4. **Date** — parse to ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` via:
+   - `date.fromisoformat` (primary)
+   - Alternate formats: `%Y/%m/%d`, `%Y_%m_%d`, `%d %b %Y`, `%b %d %Y`  
+     (ambiguous slash/dash numeric orders are deliberately excluded)
+5. **Description** — strip; empty → `__EMPTY__` placeholder constant.
+
+### Batch filtering (`validate_and_normalise_rows`)
+
+After per-row validation:
+
+| Condition | Lenient | Strict |
+|---|---|---|
+| Row validation error | `row_invalid` warning, skip row | raise `ValidationError` |
+| Duplicate `id` | `duplicate_id` warning, keep first | raise |
+| Balance marker row | `balance_row_skipped` warning, skip | raise |
+| Debit row (`debit_amount > 0`) | `non_credit_row_skipped` warning, skip | raise |
+| Neither credit nor debit | `row_invalid` warning, skip | raise |
+
+Credit rows (`credit_amount > 0`, `debit_amount == 0`) are accepted.
+
+### Early exit paths
+
+When `transactions_absence` is set by the tool layer:
+
+| Value | Warning code | Behaviour |
+|---|---|---|
+| `"missing"` | `no_transactions` | Return empty transactions, `early_exit=True` |
+| `"null"` | `no_transactions` | Return empty transactions, `early_exit=True` |
+
+## Input / output contract
+
+### Input: `BankTransactionRequest`
+
+```
+analysis_id           str
+country_region        str | None
+validation_mode       "lenient" | "strict"
+transactions          tuple[RawBankTransaction, ...]
+```
+
+Each `RawBankTransaction` carries: `id`, `date`, `description`, `debit_amount`, `credit_amount`, optional `balance`, `reference`, `page`, `line`, `is_brought_forward`, `is_final_balance`.
+
+### Output: `PayloadValidationResult`
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class PayloadValidationResult:
+    transactions: tuple[RawBankTransaction, ...]
+    warnings: tuple[ValidationWarning, ...]
+    early_exit: bool = False
+```
+
+Normalised row fields:
+
+- `date` → ISO string (`YYYY-MM-DD`)
+- `description` → stripped or `__EMPTY__`
+- amounts → `Decimal`
+
+Tool wrapper returns `ValidationToolResult` with the same fields plus optional audit data.
+
+## Confidence and warnings
+
+This phase does **not** assign confidence scores. It emits structured warnings consumed by the orchestrator and audit trail.
+
+| Warning code | When emitted |
+|---|---|
+| `schema_violation` | Invalid payload fields or jsonschema errors (tests) |
+| `no_transactions` | Missing/null transactions key |
+| `row_invalid` | Per-row validation failure (lenient) |
+| `duplicate_id` | Second row with same `id` |
+| `balance_row_skipped` | Brought-forward or final-balance marker |
+| `non_credit_row_skipped` | Debit-only row (FR-002 credit contract) |
+
+In **strict** mode, the first fatal error raises `ValidationError` instead of accumulating warnings.
+
+## Configuration
+
+No dedicated phase YAML. Behaviour is controlled by:
+
+| Key / parameter | Default | Location | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `mode` / `validation_mode` | `lenient` | request payload | `strict` fails fast on first error |
+| `EMPTY_DESCRIPTION_PLACEHOLDER` | `__EMPTY__` | `BankTransactionValidationService.py` | Module constant |
+| `_VALID_COUNTRY_REGIONS` | 4 UK regions + default | same | Frozenset |
+| `_DATE_FORMATS` | 4 alternate patterns | same | After ISO parse failure |
+| `input.schema.json` | — | `schemas/` | Test/fixture validation only |
+
+## Logging
+
+| Level | Content |
+|---|---|
+| INFO | Phase start/done via `CustomTool` (`phase=validate`) |
+| TRACE | Linearised request JSON as `tool.request {...}` |
+| DEBUG | Per-row skip reasons when lenient |
+
+Logger: `nw_agcore_bank_transactions.channels.tools.validation.BankTransactionValidationTools`.
+
+## Flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    IN[BankTransactionRequest] --> PF[validate_payload_fields]
+    PF --> ABS{transactions_absence?}
+    ABS -- missing/null --> WARN[no_transactions warning]
+    WARN --> EXIT[early_exit=True, empty transactions]
+    ABS -- present --> ROWS[validate_and_normalise_rows]
+    ROWS --> LOOP{For each row}
+    LOOP --> VAL[_validate_single]
+    VAL -- fail strict --> ERR[Raise ValidationError]
+    VAL -- fail lenient --> W1[row_invalid warning]
+    VAL -- ok --> FILT{Credit row?}
+    FILT -- duplicate id --> W2[duplicate_id warning]
+    FILT -- balance marker --> W3[balance_row_skipped]
+    FILT -- debit --> W4[non_credit_row_skipped]
+    FILT -- credit --> ACC[Accept row]
+    W1 --> LOOP
+    W2 --> LOOP
+    W3 --> LOOP
+    W4 --> LOOP
+    ACC --> LOOP
+    LOOP --> OUT[PayloadValidationResult]
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+| File | Coverage |
+|---|---|
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/validation/test_validation.py` | Lenient/strict row filtering, debit skip, duplicate ids |
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/validation/test_schema_check.py` | `input.schema.json` fixture validation |
+| `tests/unit/nw_agcore_bank_transactions/pipeline/validation/test_parse_date_formats.py` | Alternate date format acceptance |
+
+## Related modules
+
+- **Phase 2** `normalization/` — consumes validated `RawBankTransaction` rows.
+- **`../_models/`** — `RawBankTransaction`, `BankTransactionRequest`.
+- **`nw_core.validation`** — shared `ValidationWarning` type.
+
+## REST endpoint
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Tool | `run_validate_bank_transaction_payload` |
+| Method | `POST` |
+| Path | `/api/v1/validation/validate` |
+| OpenAPI | `channels/rest/routes/openapi/run_validate_bank_transaction_payload.openapi.yaml` |
+
+### Sample request
+
+```json
+{"payload":{"analysis_id":"demo","transactions":[]},"mode":"lenient"}
+```
+
+### Sample response (`result` field)
+
+```json
+{"transactions":[],"warnings":[],"early_exit":false}
+```
+
+Services are instantiated per call. REST handlers build a fresh `RouteContext` per request — do not share mutable state across threads.
