+# nw-aglib-toolkit
+
+**Package:** `nw-aglib-toolkit`  
+**Module:** `nw_aglib_toolkit`  
+**Role:** Shared framework for agent exposure, deployment, pipeline configuration, and observability.
+
+This library provides the building blocks used by core and business agents: in-process agent contracts, HTTP/in-process invocation clients, channel bootstrapping, tool registration, layered YAML configuration, and pipeline audit trails.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Architecture](#architecture)
+- [Module index](#module-index)
+- [Quick start](#quick-start)
+- [Dependencies](#dependencies)
+- [Modules](#modules)
+  - [agent — BaseAgent](#agent--baseagent)
+  - [clients — Agent invocation](#clients--agent-invocation)
+  - [pipeline.config — Layered configuration](#pipelineconfig--layered-configuration)
+  - [audit — Pipeline observability](#audit--pipeline-observability)
+  - [channels.registry_helpers — Registry assembly](#channelsregistry_helpers--registry-assembly)
+  - [channels.deployment — Bootstrap and manifests](#channelsdeployment--bootstrap-and-manifests)
+  - [channels.tools — Tool registration and discovery](#channelstools--tool-registration-and-discovery)
+  - [channels.runtime — Agent channel runtime](#channelsruntime--agent-channel-runtime)
+- [Testing](#testing)
+  - [Test layout](#test-layout)
+  - [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)
+  - [Commands](#commands)
+  - [Markers](#markers)
+  - [Coverage configuration](#coverage-configuration)
+  - [Notes](#notes)
+
+---
+
+## Architecture
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TB
+    subgraph toolkit [nw_aglib_toolkit]
+        Agent[agent.BaseAgent]
+        Clients[agent.AgentClient]
+        Config[pipeline.config]
+        Audit[audit.AuditBuilder]
+        Channels[channels]
+    end
+
+    subgraph channels_detail [channels]
+        Registry[registry_helpers]
+        Deploy[deployment]
+        Tools[tools]
+        Runtime[runtime]
+    end
+
+    subgraph consumers [Consumers]
+        CoreAgent[core agents]
+        BizAgent[business agents]
+        TemplateApp[template API]
+    end
+
+    CoreAgent --> Agent
+    CoreAgent --> Config
+    CoreAgent --> Audit
+    CoreAgent --> Channels
+    BizAgent --> Channels
+    TemplateApp --> Clients
+    TemplateApp --> Agent
+```
+
+---
+
+## Module index
+
+| Module | Description |
+|--------|-------------|
+| `agent` | In-process agent contract (`BaseAgent`) and invocation clients |
+| `agent.AgentClient` | REST / in-process agent transport |
+| `pipeline.config` | Layered YAML configuration loader |
+| `audit` | Pipeline step observability |
+| `channels.ChannelRegistryHelpers` | Channel registry assembly |
+| `channels.AgentDeployment` | Deployment manifest and bootstrap |
+| `channels.tools` | `@tool` decorator, registry, adapters |
+| `channels.AgentChannelRuntime` | Agent channel runtime |
+
+---
+
+## Quick start
+
+From the monorepo root:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-packages
+```
+
+Minimal usage:
+
+```python
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.agent import BaseAgent
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.pipeline.config import load_config
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.channels.ChannelRegistryHelpers import build_agent_channel_registry
+
+class MyAgent(BaseAgent):
+    name = "my-agent"
+
+    async def invoke(self, payload: dict) -> dict:
+        return {"echo": payload}
+
+cfg = load_config()
+registry = build_agent_channel_registry(tools_package="my_agent.channels.tools")
+```
+
+---
+
+## Dependencies
+
+| Package | Purpose |
+|---------|---------|
+| `nw-core` | Channel base types, REST factory, deployment primitives |
+| `httpx` | REST agent client |
+| `pyyaml` | Configuration loading |
+| `fastapi` / `uvicorn` | Channel bootstrap |
+| `grpcio` (optional) | gRPC channel support |
+
+---
+
+## Modules
+
+### agent — BaseAgent
+
+#### Description
+
+`BaseAgent` is the abstract in-process contract for agent logic. It defines a single `invoke()` method and carries no network I/O. Agents subclass this type to expose domain logic that can be embedded in an application or wrapped by an `InProcessAgentClient`.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Implement agent business logic in a deployable service
+- Embed an agent directly in a host application (no HTTP hop)
+- Register agent methods as tools via `ChannelToolRegistry.register_from_agent()`
+
+#### Configuration
+
+None. Subclasses define their own `name` attribute and `invoke()` behaviour.
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from typing import Any
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.agent import BaseAgent
+
+
+class EchoAgent(BaseAgent):
+    name = "echo-agent"
+
+    async def invoke(self, payload: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
+        return {"echo": payload}
+
+
+agent = EchoAgent()
+result = await agent.invoke({"message": "hello"})
+# {"echo": {"message": "hello"}}
+```
+
+---
+
+### clients — Agent invocation
+
+#### Description
+
+The `clients` package provides transport abstractions for invoking agents. `AgentClient` is the abstract base; concrete implementations call agents over HTTP (`RestAgentClient`) or in-process (`InProcessAgentClient`).
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Switch between embedded and remote agent invocation based on deployment mode
+- Call a deployed agent's `POST /invoke` endpoint from a host application
+- Delegate to an in-process `BaseAgent` instance without HTTP overhead
+
+#### Configuration
+
+| Client | Parameter | Default | Purpose |
+|--------|-----------|---------|---------|
+| `RestAgentClient` | `base_url` | required | Agent service base URL (trailing slash stripped) |
+| `RestAgentClient` | `timeout` | `30.0` | HTTP request timeout in seconds |
+| `InProcessAgentClient` | `agent` | required | Object with `async invoke(payload)` method |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.agent import AgentClient, InProcessAgentClient, RestAgentClient
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.agent import BaseAgent
+
+
+class EchoAgent(BaseAgent):
+    name = "echo"
+
+    async def invoke(self, payload: dict) -> dict:
+        return {"echo": payload}
+
+
+# In-process (embedded mode)
+client: AgentClient = InProcessAgentClient(EchoAgent())
+result = await client.invoke({"msg": "hi"})
+
+# Remote (REST mode)
+client = RestAgentClient("http://localhost:8080", timeout=10.0)
+result = await client.invoke({"msg": "hi"})
+```
+
+---
+
+### pipeline.config — Layered configuration
+
+#### Description
+
+`pipeline.config` loads and merges YAML configuration from multiple sources into a single `AppConfig` object. Built-in defaults come from toolkit and domain packages; callers can layer file overrides and runtime dict overrides on top.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Provide deterministic, versioned pipeline parameters (weights, thresholds, keywords)
+- Apply per-request or per-bank configuration overlays
+- Access typed convenience methods instead of raw dict lookups
+
+#### Configuration
+
+##### Load layers (lowest to highest priority)
+
+1. Built-in YAML defaults (toolkit `versions.yaml` + domain package configs)
+2. `file_overrides` — list of YAML file paths
+3. `overrides` — caller-supplied dict
+4. `source_bank` — optional bank-specific overlay (e.g. `"natwest"`, `"barclays"`)
+
+##### Key types
+
+| Symbol | Purpose |
+|--------|---------|
+| `load_config()` | Build merged `AppConfig` |
+| `AppConfig` | Frozen wrapper with accessor methods |
+| `ConfigLoadError` | YAML or validation failure |
+| `deep_merge()` | Recursive dict merge utility |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.pipeline.config import load_config, deep_merge
+
+# Defaults only
+cfg = load_config()
+high_threshold = cfg.threshold("high")
+weights = cfg.weight("date_pattern_score")
+
+# File + caller overrides
+cfg = load_config(
+    file_overrides=[Path("config/override.yaml")],
+    overrides={"thresholds": {"high": 0.90}},
+    source_bank="barclays",
+)
+
+# Standalone merge
+merged = deep_merge({"a": {"b": 1}}, {"a": {"c": 2}})
+```
+
+---
+
+### audit — Pipeline observability
+
+#### Description
+
+`AuditBuilder` collects deterministic step records, timings, and optional feature/candidate snapshots during pipeline execution. When disabled, all methods are no-ops and `snapshot()` returns `None`.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Trace pipeline phase inputs/outputs for debugging or compliance
+- Record config versions and effective kwargs alongside results
+- Attach audit snapshots to API responses when callers request audit data
+
+#### Configuration
+
+| Field | Default | Purpose |
+|-------|---------|---------|
+| `enabled` | `False` | Master switch; when `False`, builder is a no-op |
+| `analysis_id` | `""` | Correlation ID in the audit snapshot |
+| `config_versions` | `{}` | Version stamps from merged config |
+| `effective_kwargs` | `{}` | Runtime parameters used for the analysis |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.audit import AuditBuilder
+
+audit = AuditBuilder(enabled=True, analysis_id="run-001")
+
+audit.start_step("feature_extraction")
+# ... run phase ...
+audit.record_step(
+    "feature_extraction",
+    input_summary={"count": 42},
+    output_summary={"features": 42},
+)
+
+snapshot = audit.snapshot()
+if snapshot:
+    print(snapshot.pipeline_steps[0].name)
+    print(snapshot.timings_ms)
+```
+
+---
+
+### channels.registry_helpers — Registry assembly
+
+#### Description
+
+Helpers for assembling standard agent channel registries from optional REST router, tools package, gRPC servicer, and MQ handler inputs.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Wire up REST + tools channels in agent `channels/registry.py`
+- Discover `@tool`-decorated functions from a Python package automatically
+- Build a `ChannelRegistry` without duplicating boilerplate per agent
+
+#### Configuration
+
+| Function | Parameters | Purpose |
+|----------|------------|---------|
+| `register_tools_from_package(package_name)` | Package dotted path | Returns a callback that registers discovered tools |
+| `build_agent_channel_registry(...)` | `rest_router`, `tools_package`, `grpc_servicer`, `mq_handler`, `mq_adapter` | Builds `ChannelRegistry` from enabled modules |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from fastapi import APIRouter
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.channels.ChannelRegistryHelpers import build_agent_channel_registry
+
+router = APIRouter()
+registry = build_agent_channel_registry(
+    rest_router=router,
+    rest_prefix="/api/v1",
+    tools_package="my_agent.channels.tools",
+)
+```
+
+---
+
+### channels.deployment — Bootstrap and manifests
+
+#### Description
+
+Agent-specific deployment types and bootstrap logic built on `nw_core.channels.ChannelDeployment`. Loads YAML deployment manifests, composes embedded core agents, and assembles a FastAPI application with channel runtime.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Load `config/deployment.yaml` for an agent
+- Bootstrap standalone or composite deployments with embedded core agents
+- Create a runnable FastAPI app from a `ChannelRegistry`
+
+#### Configuration
+
+Deployment YAML fields (via `AgentDeploymentManifest.load()`):
+
+| Field | Purpose |
+|-------|---------|
+| `unit` | Deployment unit name |
+| `mode` | `standalone` or composite mode |
+| `channels` | Per-channel enable flags |
+| `embedded_core` | In-process core agent wiring |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.channels.AgentDeployment import (
+    AgentChannelBootstrap,
+    AgentDeploymentManifest,
+)
+
+manifest = AgentDeploymentManifest.load(Path("config/deployment.yaml"))
+app = AgentChannelBootstrap.build(manifest=manifest, registry=registry)
+```
+
+---
+
+### channels.tools — Tool registration and discovery
+
+#### Description
+
+The tools channel exposes pipeline functions as LLM-callable tools. The `@tool` decorator marks functions with metadata; `PipelineToolRegistry` and `ChannelToolRegistry` manage registration; adapters bridge to LangChain, MCP, Strands, and internal formats.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Decorate pipeline service methods for tools-channel exposure
+- Auto-discover tools from a Python package
+- Bridge a pipeline registry into the channel tool registry
+
+#### Configuration
+
+`@tool` decorator parameters:
+
+| Parameter | Default | Purpose |
+|-----------|---------|---------|
+| `name` | function name | Tool identifier |
+| `description` | function docstring | Tool description for LLM callers |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.channels.tools import tool, PipelineToolRegistry
+
+
+@tool(description="Group transactions into skeletons")
+async def run_skeleton_grouping(transactions: list[dict]) -> dict:
+    return {"groups": []}
+
+
+registry = PipelineToolRegistry()
+registry.register_instance_methods(SkeletonTools())
+tools = registry.list()
+```
+
+See also `InternalToolAdapter` for bridging `PipelineToolRegistry` into `ChannelToolRegistry`.
+
+---
+
+### channels.runtime — Agent channel runtime
+
+#### Description
+
+`AgentChannelRuntime` extends `nw_core.channels.ChannelModules.ChannelRuntime` with an optional `ChannelToolRegistry` reference for agents that expose a tools channel.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Hold tool registry state alongside other channel modules during runtime
+- Access registered tools from channel handlers at request time
+
+#### Configuration
+
+None. The runtime is constructed by `AgentChannelBootstrap` during deployment assembly.
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from nw_aglib_toolkit.channels.AgentChannelRuntime import AgentChannelRuntime
+
+runtime = AgentChannelRuntime()
+runtime.tool_registry = channel_tool_registry
+```
+
+---
+
+## Testing
+
+### Test layout
+
+Test files use Java-style PascalCase names aligned with source modules: `{Module}Test.py` (e.g. `BaseAgent.py` → `BaseAgentTest.py`).
+
+```
+tests/
+├── unit/          # Isolated unit tests (@pytest.mark.unit)
+├── feature/       # Component feature tests (@pytest.mark.feature)
+└── tools/         # Tool channel tests
+```
+
+| Test file | Source module |
+|-----------|---------------|
+| `unit/BaseAgentTest.py` | `agent/BaseAgent.py` |
+| `unit/AgentClientTest.py` | `agent/AgentClient.py` |
+| `unit/ConfigLoaderTest.py` | `pipeline/config/ConfigLoader.py` |
+| `unit/AuditBuilderTest.py` | `audit/AuditBuilder.py` |
+| `unit/ChannelRegistryHelpersTest.py` | `channels/ChannelRegistryHelpers.py` |
+| `feature/AgentClientRestTest.py` | `agent/AgentClient.py` (REST round-trip) |
+| `tools/ToolAnnotationsTest.py` | `channels/tools/ToolAnnotations.py` |
+| `tools/ToolDiscoveryTest.py` | `channels/tools/ToolDiscovery.py` |
+| `tools/ToolRegistryTest.py` | `channels/tools/ToolRegistry.py` |
+| `tools/InternalToolAdapterTest.py` | `channels/tools/adapters/InternalToolAdapter.py` |
+| `tools/ToolTraceLoggingTest.py` | `channels/tools/ToolAnnotations.py` (TRACE logging) |
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+From the monorepo root:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-packages
+```
+
+Or from this package directory (includes dev dependencies for coverage, async tests, and bank-transactions config fixtures):
+
+```bash
+cd libs/agents/toolkit
+uv sync --group dev
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+Run from `libs/agents/toolkit`:
+
+```bash
+# Unit tests only
+uv run pytest tests/unit -m unit
+
+# Feature tests only
+uv run pytest tests/feature -m feature
+
+# Tool channel tests
+uv run pytest tests/tools
+
+# All toolkit tests
+uv run pytest
+
+# Coverage report (unit + feature + tools)
+uv run pytest --cov=nw_aglib_toolkit --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=html
+```
+
+After a coverage run, open `htmlcov/index.html` for the HTML report.
+
+### Markers
+
+| Marker | Purpose |
+|--------|---------|
+| `unit` | Fast, isolated tests with mocks/monkeypatch |
+| `feature` | Component-level tests with minimal wiring (e.g. ASGI app + HTTP client) |
+
+Root monorepo markers (`smoke`, `e2e`, etc.) are defined in the workspace `pyproject.toml` but are not used in this package's test suite.
+
+### Coverage configuration
+
+Coverage is configured in `pyproject.toml`:
+
+- **Source:** `nw_aglib_toolkit`
+- **Branch coverage:** enabled
+- **Omitted:** `__init__.py` files and test directories
+- **Report:** missing lines shown in terminal; HTML report generated with `--cov-report=html`
+
+Target modules for meaningful coverage:
+
+- `pipeline.config` — config loading and merge logic
+- `clients` — REST and in-process invocation
+- `agent` — BaseAgent contract
+- `audit` — AuditBuilder step recording
+- `channels.registry_helpers` — registry assembly
+- `channels.tools` — tool registration and discovery
+
+### Notes
+
+- Config loader tests that call `load_config()` without overrides require `nw-agcore-bank-transactions` (declared as a dev dependency) for built-in YAML defaults.
+- Tests use `pythonpath = ["src"]` from this package's `pyproject.toml`.
+- Pytest discovers `*Test.py` and `test_*.py` files (`python_files` in `pyproject.toml`).
