+---
+
+## Modules
+
+### channels — Channel modules and deployment
+
+#### Description
+
+Provides the channel abstraction layer: registry of REST/gRPC/MQ modules, deployment manifest loading from YAML, and runtime assembly into a FastAPI app (when REST is enabled).
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Load `config/deployment.yaml` and enable channels per component
+- Register REST routers, gRPC servicers, and MQ handlers
+- Bootstrap a runnable channel runtime shared by agents and apps
+
+#### Configuration
+
+Deployment YAML (`DeploymentManifest.load()`):
+
+| Field | Purpose |
+|-------|---------|
+| `unit` | Deployment unit name |
+| `mode` | `standalone` or composite mode |
+| `channels` | Per-channel `enabled` and `prefix` flags |
+| `embedded_core` | Embedded core agent channel rules |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from fastapi import APIRouter
+from nw_core.channels.ChannelDeployment import ChannelBootstrap, DeploymentManifest
+from nw_core.channels.ChannelModules import ChannelRegistry, RestChannelModule
+
+manifest = DeploymentManifest(
+    unit="my-agent",
+    channels={"rest": {"enabled": True, "prefix": "/api/v1"}},
+)
+registry = ChannelRegistry()
+registry.add(RestChannelModule(APIRouter()))
+runtime = ChannelBootstrap.build(manifest, registry, title="My Agent")
+```
+
+#### REST factory
+
+```python
+from nw_core.channels.rest.RestFactory import create_fastapi_app, mount_router
+
+app = create_fastapi_app(title="My Service")
+# mount_router(app, router, prefix="/api")
+```
+
+---
+
+### config — Component settings
+
+#### Description
+
+Loads typed settings from `config/env.{NW_ENV}` with optional `.env.local` override. `BaseComponentSettings` covers host, port, log level, and gRPC port; `AppComponentSettings` adds HTTP client defaults.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Standardize environment configuration across agents and apps
+- Resolve component root from a module `__file__` path
+
+#### Configuration
+
+| Setting | Env var | Default |
+|---------|---------|---------|
+| `nw_env` | `NW_ENV` | `dev` |
+| `log_level` | `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` |
+| `host` | `HOST` | `127.0.0.1` |
+| `port` | `PORT` | `8000` |
+| `grpc_port` | `GRPC_PORT` | `50051` |
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+from nw_core.config.ComponentSettings import BaseComponentSettings, load_settings
+
+settings = load_settings(Path("/path/to/component"), BaseComponentSettings, env="dev")
+print(settings.host, settings.port)
+```
+
+---
+
+### logging — Structured logging
+
+#### Description
+
+Extends Python logging with a custom `TRACE` level (below DEBUG), call-context injection (`unique_id`, `analysis_id`), and the `@LogFn` decorator for structured call/return logging with accurate source locations.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Emit verbose pipeline diagnostics at TRACE without flooding INFO logs
+- Correlate log lines to detector calls and analysis IDs
+- Wrap tool/service entry points with consistent timing logs
+
+#### Configuration
+
+Call `setup_trace()` once at process start to register the TRACE level.
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+import logging
+from nw_core.logging import TRACE, LogFn, get_logger, setup_trace
+
+setup_trace()
+logger = get_logger(__name__)
+
+@LogFn(logger=logger)
+def run_phase(data: dict) -> dict:
+    logger.log(TRACE, "detail %s", data)
+    return {"ok": True}
+```
+
+---
+
+### calendar — UK working-day calendar
+
+#### Description
+
+`WorkingDayCalendar` calculates UK working days using the `holidays` library, with optional region overrides from pipeline config.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Salary/recurrence date tolerance calculations
+- Last/next working day lookups for bank-transaction pipelines
+
+#### Configuration
+
+Regions: `EnglandAndWales`, `Scotland`, `NorthernIreland`. Override layers via `CalendarOverrides.from_config()`.
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from datetime import date
+from nw_core.calendar import WorkingDayCalendar, working_day_calendar_from_app_config
+
+calendar = WorkingDayCalendar()
+calendar.is_working_day(date(2024, 1, 8), "EnglandAndWales")
+
+cfg = load_config()  # AppConfig-like object
+calendar = working_day_calendar_from_app_config(cfg)
+```
+
+---
+
+### validation — Schema checking
+
+#### Description
+
+Shared `ValidationWarning` model and `SchemaCheckService` for JSON-schema validation with strict or warn-only modes.
+
+#### Use case
+
+- Validate pipeline payloads against packaged JSON schemas
+- Collect non-fatal warnings instead of raising when configured
+
+#### Configuration
+
+`SchemaCheckConfig`: `enabled`, `strict` flags control validation behaviour.
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from nw_core.validation import SchemaCheckService, ValidationWarning
+
+schema = {"type": "object", "properties": {"id": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["id"]}
+service = SchemaCheckService(schema)
+result = service.check({"id": "t1"})
+assert result.valid
+```
+
+---
+
+### grpc — Protobuf JSON helpers
+
+#### Description
+
+Thin wrappers around `google.protobuf.json_format` for converting protobuf messages to/from dicts (used by gRPC detect handlers).
+
+#### Sample usage
+
+```python
+from google.protobuf.struct_pb2 import Struct
+from nw_core.grpc.ProtoJson import dict_to_message, message_to_dict
+
+message = Struct()
+dict_to_message({"key": "value"}, message)
+data = message_to_dict(message)
+```
+
+---
+
+## gRPC contracts
+
+Cross-agent protobuf message types and generated Python stubs for gRPC channels.
+
+| Path | Role |
+|------|------|
+| `channels/grpc/proto/nw/bank_transactions/v1/` | Shared bank-transaction DTOs (`common`, `hints`, `results`) |
+| `channels/grpc/proto/nw/common/v1/` | Cross-cutting primitives (`health.proto`) |
+| `channels/grpc/generated/` | Python `*_pb2.py` output from `scripts/generate_grpc.sh` |
+| `channels/grpc/GrpcServer.py` | gRPC server bootstrap (`serve_grpc`, `run_grpc_server`) |
+
+Business agents keep service-specific protos under:
+
+`agents/business/<agent>/src/<pkg>/channels/grpc/proto/nw/<agent>/v1/`
+
+Regenerate stubs:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/generate_grpc.sh
+```
